<t4htlink 
 href="#x1-2xdoc" name="x1-2xdoc"></t4htlink>
<!--l. 1--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><t4htlink 
 href="#likesection.2" name="likesection.2"></t4htlink><t4htlink 
 href="#x1-10x" name="x1-10x"></t4htlink></text:p> 
<text:section text:style-name="begin-end-env" text:name="begin-end-env-2" ><text:p text:style-name="begin-env-p" ></text:p><!--begin center-->
<text:p text:style-name="center" >
 <text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1728">Petition for Permanent Residency under Extraordinary</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1728">ability (EB-1A)</text:span></text:span>
</text:p><text:p text:style-name="end-env-p" ></text:p></text:section><!--end center-->
<!--l. 5--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"></text:p> 
 <table:table  
table:style-name="tabular" ><!--table:table-column-group ???="TBL-1-1g"--><table:table-column 
table:style-name="TBL-1-1" 
/><table:table-column 
table:style-name="TBL-1-2" 
/><!--/table:table-column-group--><table:table-row  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-1-"><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-1-1"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  <text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Petitioner and Beneficiary:</text:span></text:span> </text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-1-2"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  Taximov Askar                                               </text:p></table:table-cell>
</table:table-row><table:table-row  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-2-"><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-2-1"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  <text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Classification Sought:</text:span></text:span>         </text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-2-2"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  Employment-Based Immigration, First Preference  </text:p></table:table-cell>
</table:table-row><table:table-row  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-3-"><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-3-1"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >                                             </text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-3-2"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  Extraordinary Ability in Science (EB-1A)            </text:p></table:table-cell>
</table:table-row><table:table-row  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-4-"><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-4-1"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >                                             </text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-4-2"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  Sec. 203(b)(1) INA [8 U.S.C. 1153]                     </text:p></table:table-cell>
</table:table-row><table:table-row  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-5-"><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-5-1"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  <text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Type of Petition:</text:span></text:span>               </text:p></table:table-cell><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-1-5-2"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >  I-140                                                            </text:p></table:table-cell>
</table:table-row></table:table>
<!--l. 15--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Dear Immigration Officer,
</text:p> 
<!--l. 17--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">This following evidence is respectfully submitted in support of the petition of Mr. Taximov Askar  for
classification as a qualified immigrant under the first preference employment immigration for Aliens of
Extraordinary Ability pursuant to section 203(b)(1)(A) of the Immigration and Nationality
Act.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 22--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Specifically, the evidence shows that:
      </text:p> 
<text:list text:style-name="Enumerate" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Summary of Mr. Taximov’s achievements and qualifications
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Mr. Taximov satisfies <text:span text:style-name="underline" >nine</text:span> of the ten criteria listed in 8 CFR, Section 204.5(h)(3), namely:
           </text:p> 
<text:list text:style-name="Enumerate" > 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s receipt of lesser nationally or internationally recognized
           prizes or awards for excellence [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">2.1<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">8<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>].
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s membership in associations in the field which demand
           outstanding achievement of their members [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-100002.2">2.2<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Associations --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-100002.2">20<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Associations --></t4htlink>].
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence of published material about Mr. Taximov in professional or major media
           relating to his work [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-120002.3">2.3<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Published --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-120002.3">22<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Published --></t4htlink>].
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence that Mr. Taximov has been asked to judge the work of others on a panel
           [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4">2.4<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Judging --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4">25<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Judging --></t4htlink>].
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s original scientific, business-related contributions of major
           significance to the field [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">2.5<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">36<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>].
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s authorship of scholarly articles in the field, in professional
           or major trade publications or other major media [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6">2.6<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Articles --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6">51<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Articles --></t4htlink>]
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Comparable evidence of public display of work (IT Project Management) [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-320002.8">2.8<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Display --></t4htlink>,
           page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-320002.8">74<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Display --></t4htlink>]
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s performance of a critical role in distinguished organizations
           [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-270002.7">2.7<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Role --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-270002.7">55<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Role --></t4htlink>].
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Evidence that Mr. Taximov commands a high salary in relation to others in the field
           [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-330002.9">2.9<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Salary --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-330002.9">78<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Salary --></t4htlink>].
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

      </text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Mr. Taximov is one of that small percentage who has risen to the very top of the field
      of IT Project Management and he has sustained international acclaim [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-340003">3<!--tex4ht:ref: sec:Merits --></t4htlink>,
      page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-340003">82<!--tex4ht:ref: sec:Merits --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-enumerate" >Mr. Taximov’s work will substantially benefit the United States [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-370004">4<!--tex4ht:ref: sec:Benefit --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-370004">87<!--tex4ht:ref: sec:Benefit --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 75--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Pursuant to 8 CFR, Section 204.5(h)(1), Mr. Taximov may file an I-140 visa petition for classification
under Section 203(b)(1)(A) of the Act as an alien of extraordinary ability in science on his own
behalf.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 80--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Pursuant to 8 CFR, Section 204.5(h)(5), neither an offer for employment in the United States nor a
labor certification is required for this classification.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              

</text:p> 
<!--start of section--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-2" text:outline-level="2" ><text:span text:style-name="section" >1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-10001" name="x1-10001"></t4htlink>Summary of Mr. Taximov’s achievements and qualifications</text:h> 

<!--l. 43--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In this petition, Mr. Taximov is presented as an IT Project Manager who has been overseeing the
creation and implementation of IT, innovative, Building Information Modelling (BIM), and urban
technology systems for more than 10 years. His work encompasses architectural design, workflow
configuration, development management, and product logic formation, enabling the solutions he creates
to function reliably in the daily operations of educational, business and government organizations. In
2008 he graduated from Eurasian National University with honors and he got a Bachelor’s degree in
Construction with specialization in Civil Engineering. In 2015 he earned his Master’s degree in Building
and Urban Design in Development at University College London (UCL). His Master’s degree
dissertation on affordable housing was focused on using IT framework, such as (SDSS) Spatial Decision
Support System.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 48--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Kakhar Kashimov. CTO, Chief Software Architect, “KazDream Technologies” LLC</text:span>. An independent
industry expert further confirms that this research-driven foundation translated into practical,
nationally relevant urban technology solutions. Kakhar Kashimov states:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 50--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="textit" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I believe that Askar’s innovative mindset reflects not only his professional experience but</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">also his scientific approach, which he developed through his research work on creating a new</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">mechanism for determining the necessity of constructing social infrastructure facilities such as</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">schools, kindergartens, and residential complexes, using geographic information systems (GIS)</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and the architecture of Spatial Decision Support Systems (SDSS). In his scientific work, he</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">proposed a unique IT solution to address the problem of inaccurate forecasting and planning of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">socially significant infrastructure development across the country. I am confident that his IT</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">developments in the field of social infrastructure and industrial system design significantly</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">influence the scaling of information technologies and remain highly relevant and practical</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">today”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 52--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In 2018 he joined the Nazarbayev University Research and Innovation System (NURIS) as a Director of
Technopark. During that period he improved Technopark as an attractive place for startup companies,
small and medium enterprises (SME) by bringing industrial experts, researchers, technology
entrepreneurs and investors together. His next joint IT project was the “Life Signal” service for Android
and iOS platforms, developed with the participation of Google and Apple, and aimed at emergency
response and interaction of 112 operational services with citizens’ calls, including rational allocation and
use of emergency-service resources.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 55--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">From 2019 to 2021, while working at Astana Innovations, the company responsible for Smart City
concept integration Big Data urban platform, the creation of analytical models, and the transition from
open data to industrial API services, he was involved in the development of IT solutions that form
the basis for the automation of interdepartmental processes and the creation of services
for city residents. From March to June 2022, his work at Elorda Qurylys Kompaniyasy, a
municipal developer with a public mandate to complete problematic shared construction
projects, included the implementation of digital systems for managing budgets, processes, and
construction cycles, which required a combination of IT architecture, automation, and management
tools. At the same time, starting on January 18, 2022, as an Independent Director of the
National Cybersecurity operator “State Technical Service” JSC, he participated in strategic
oversight and expert work on platforms that protect e-Government and critical information
systems.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 57--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov is currently a Head, IT Project Manager at iKOMEK109 which is similar to the Office of
Unified Communications 311 (non-emergency services) in the United States cities. Mr. Taximov joined
iKOMEK109 in May 2022, after getting a solid experience in IT sector and his career centers on IT
Project Management, Innovations and cybersecurity in government and enterprises. His
résumé Exhibit here and diplomas Exhibit here are included. Across roles, he has delivered (i)
omnichannel civic-service platforms, (ii) election-grade address/registry data pipelines, (iii) national
cybersecurity-operations tooling, (iv) computer-vision deployments at city scale and (v) enterprise
digitalization programs.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 59--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The documents reflect official recognition of his activities, including letters of appreciation from the
President of the Republic of Kazakhstan for organizing the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO)
international summit, conducting presidential and parliamentary elections, numerous awards from
government agencies, and recognition from Kaspersky for his contribution to information security
[Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">2.1<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">8<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>]. Separately, there is confirmation that he was awarded the Bolashak state
scholarship to study at UCL, which became the basis for his further professional work in the field of IT
Project Management [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-50002.1.2">2.1.2<!--tex4ht:ref: subsubsec:BolashakStipend --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-50002.1.2">10<!--tex4ht:ref: subsubsec:BolashakStipend --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 61--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">His professional status is reinforced by his membership in the Kazakhstan Information Security
Association, where he was accepted by decision of the Council after verification of compliance
with the established requirements for professional experience and qualifications [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-100002.2">2.2<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Associations --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-100002.2">20<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Associations --></t4htlink>]. The media has repeatedly covered his work on urban systems, digital platforms, and
processes for handling requests from residents of the capital [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-120002.3">2.3<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Published --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-120002.3">22<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Published --></t4htlink>]. The
materials also include translations of these publications and data on the reliability of the
sources.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 63--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">A significant part of his professional activity is his work as an expert evaluating projects and scientific
research. He is a reviewer at the Universities, a member of the jury for national programs, and a
participant in expert commissions at Kaspersky, the city situation center, and the National Security
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
operator. Written conclusions on various materials and proposals are presented, confirming the trust in
his professional opinion and the importance of expert assessment in decision-making [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4">2.4<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Judging --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4">25<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Judging --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 65--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The results of his achievements are related to the creation and launch of technological solutions that are
successfully used in city services and government structures. These include the iKOMEK109 system,
which provides round-the-clock operation and reception of calls from citizens to the unified contact
center of the Astana City Administration via telephone number 109 and alternative digital channels, as
well as a completely updated version of the iKOMEK 2.0 platform, whose architecture and functionality
were developed under his leadership and confirmed in documents and published materials [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-250002.5.4">2.5.4<!--tex4ht:ref: subsubsec:Authorship --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-250002.5.4">50<!--tex4ht:ref: subsubsec:Authorship --></t4htlink>] [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6">2.6<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Articles --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6">51<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Articles --></t4htlink>] [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-320002.8">2.8<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Display --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-320002.8">74<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Display --></t4htlink>]. A significant milestone was the introduction of
the Geonomics information system, which enabled the city of Astana to achieve maximum accuracy in
compiling voter lists within its territory by bringing together address data on citizens’ places of
residence into a single structure, as reflected in publications and confirmed by independent
sources [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-70002.1.4">2.1.4<!--tex4ht:ref: subsubsec:Awards4 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-70002.1.4">15<!--tex4ht:ref: subsubsec:Awards4 --></t4htlink>]. The materials also include projects on computer vision,
telematics, and network monitoring, under which solutions that have proven their practical value
were created and implemented under his leadership [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">2.5<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">36<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>], [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-270002.7">2.7<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Role --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-270002.7">55<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Role --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 67--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Also presented are his scientific articles on urban analytics, data management, digital services, and
security issues, published in peer-reviewed journals from the Higher Attestation Commission
list.
</text:p> 
<!--end of section--><!--start of section--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-2" text:outline-level="2" ><text:span text:style-name="section" >2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-20002" name="x1-20002"></t4htlink>Initial Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s Extraordinary Ability</text:h> 


<!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1" name="x1-30002.1"></t4htlink>Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s receipt of lesser nationally or internationally recognized prizes or
awards for excellence</text:h> 


<!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.1.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-40002.1.1" name="x1-40002.1.1"></t4htlink>Medal “Eren enbegi ushin” (<text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">For Distinguished Labour</text:span></text:span>). The Republic of Kazakhstan,
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
2025</text:h> 

<!--l. 7--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">On 21 October 2025, Mr. Taximov was awarded the state medal <text:span text:style-name="underline" >“Eren enbegi ushin”</text:span> (<text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">For Distinguished</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Labour</text:span></text:span>) by Presidential Decree. The certificate and medal set were received, both personally issued to
Mr. Taximov [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38005r1">1<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38005r1">94<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo1 --></t4htlink>][Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38009r2">2<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo2 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38009r2">97<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo2 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 9--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov was awarded in recognition of sustained labour achievements in public service and the
socio-economic sphere through long-term leadership of large-scale IT projects. Over multiple years, his
work in IT project management delivered measurable improvements in the reliability, resilience, and
security of mission-critical government and municipal digital systems that support day-to-day public
services. These outcomes reflect not only technical and managerial excellence in IT program
delivery, but also direct public benefit, including stronger reliability of digital services, faster
incident handling, and improved protection of information infrastructure relied upon by
citizens and state bodies. The award therefore aligns with the medal’s statutory purpose of
recognizing labour achievements in fields including public service and the economic and social
spheres.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 11--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Under the Law <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">On State Awards of the Republic of Kazakhstan</text:span></text:span> (12 December 1995, <text:span 
text:style-name="tcrm-1200">№ </text:span>2676)
</text:p> 
<!--l. 14--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 15--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >State  awards  are  conferred  by  the  President  to  citizens,  and  where  applicable,  foreign
      nationals, in recognition of services to the Republic and labour feats. (Art. 1, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">awarded by</text:span>
      <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the President, national scope</text:span></text:span>)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >State awards are insignia of the highest distinctions, comprising orders, medals and honorary
      titles. Names of state awards are established in the state language and their descriptions
      and certificate forms are approved by the President. (Arts. 2–3)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The list of medals of the Republic of Kazakhstan expressly includes “Eren enbegi ushin”.
      (Art. 18)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The  “Eren  enbegi  ushin”  medal  is  awarded  to  citizens  for  labour  achievements  in  the
      economic and social spheres, science, culture and public service. (Art. 21)</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 24--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Article 1.</text:span></text:span> <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Citizens of the Republic of Kazakhstan, in recognition of their services to the Republic and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">their fruitful state, social, creative and professional activities, labour feats and feats of arms, shall be</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">awarded state awards”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 26--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Article 2.</text:span></text:span> <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“State awards of the Republic of Kazakhstan shall be insignia of the highest degree of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">distinction, the order “Altyn Kyran”, the title “Halyk Kaharmany”, “Kazakhstannyn Enbek Eri”, as well</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">as other orders, medals, and honorary titles”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 28--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Article 3.</text:span></text:span> <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Names of state awards of the Republic of Kazakhstan are established in the state language.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Descriptions of state awards, samples of “Altyn Kyran”, “Halyk Kaharmany” and “Kazakstannyn Enbek</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Eri” books, order books, certificates of medals and bestowal of honorary titles, the method of nomination</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">for and bestowal of state awards, other documents, and rules, are approved by the President of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Republic of Kazakhstan”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 30--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Article 18.</text:span></text:span> <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Medals of the Republic of Kazakhstan are </text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">… ‘Eren enbegi ushin‘ ”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 32--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Article 21.</text:span></text:span> <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“The “Eren enbegi ushin” medal is awarded to citizens for labour achievements in economic</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and social spheres, science, culture and public service”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 34--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Public statement about this medal describes it as recognition for contributions to socio-economic
development and for services to society and the state, which matches the nature of Mr. Taximov’s
public-sector IT impact. This is a national, presidential state award written into law and listed among
the medals of the Republic of Kazakhstan. It is conferred by the President and recognizes excellence in
labour achievements across nationally important fields. The statutory framework (Arts. 1–3, 18, 21) and
the certificate together demonstrate that the medal is a nationally recognized prize for excellence.
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38005r1">1<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38005r1">94<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo1 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38009r2">2<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo2 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38009r2">97<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ErenEnbegi_Photo2 --></t4htlink>]

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.1.2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-50002.1.2" name="x1-50002.1.2"></t4htlink>“Bolashak” International Scholarship. Established by the President of the Republic of
Kazakhstan</text:h> 

<!--l. 40--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Bolashak International Scholarship of the President of the Republic of Kazakhstan was established
by Presidential Decree on November 5, 1993, initiated by the First President of Kazakhstan, Nursultan
Nazarbayev. The program aims to develop highly qualified personnel in priority economic sectors by
funding advanced academic studies and internships abroad. The scholarship operates according to
Government resolutions that approve the Rules for selecting candidates for the Bolashak scholarship. By
Presidential Decree No. 1569 dated May 4, 2005, the Government of the Republic of Kazakhstan was
mandated to approve the Rules for selection of applicants for the award of the Bolashak
International Scholarship. Additionally, Government Decree No. 301 dated April 4, 2005,
established the Joint Stock Company “Center for International Programs” (CIP) to administer the
program.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 42--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In 2013, the JSC “Center for International Programs” (CIP) issued two letters confirming that Mr.
Askar Taximov is a recipient of the Bolashak International Scholarship. One of the letters is addressed
to University College London (UCL) and the other is for the British Embassy Office for visa processing.
Each letter is signed by the President of CIP and shows the funded Master degree, with
major Building and Urban Design in Development from 23 September 2013 to 22 September
2014.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 44--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In order to receive the Presidential Scholarship, Mr. Taximov had to pass a complex and competitive
process of selection. The Bolashak program’s selection process is competitive, strict and merit based. It
consists of three separate rounds.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 46--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Round 1. Comprehensive Testing</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 48--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The testing process evaluates the candidate’s ability to analyze and comprehend information within a
constrained time limit. Candidates need to complete three online assessments with audio and video
monitoring
</text:p> 
<!--l. 51--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 52--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Verbal Reasoning
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Numerical Reasoning
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Personality Assessment</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 57--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Only the candidates who met the minimum threshold score proceed to Round 2. No retesting is
allowed.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 59--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Round 2. Expert Commission Interview</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 61--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Expert Commission assesses each candidate’s professional preparation and suitability for the
scholarship by conducting an anonymous personal interview. The assessment focuses on the
applicant’s level of professional training, theoretical knowledge, and professional competencies in
the chosen field of specialization. The Commission members provide recommendations for
each applicant, taking into account the information provided in the applicant’s motivation
letter.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 63--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Round 3. Republican Commission Decision</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 65--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Republican Commission for Training Personnel Abroad operates as an advisory and consultative
body to the President of the Republic of Kazakhstan. It was established under Presidential Decree No.
470 of October 12, 2000. The Commission is responsible for supervising the implementation of the
Bolashak International Scholarship. It has members who are appointed directly by the President. The
Commission’s chairman is the State Counselor of the Republic of Kazakhstan, the Minister of
Science and Higher Education serves as Deputy Chairperson, and the Vice-minister serves as
Secretary.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 67--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Applicants’ materials for the third round are submitted to the Republican Commission for Training
Personnel Abroad, along with the results of comprehensive testing and recommendations from the
Independent Expert Commission (IEC). In the third round, the Republican Commission
reviews the results of the first and second rounds and makes a final decision on the award
or refusal to award the Bolashak scholarship, which is communicated to the applicant by
posting information on the administrator’s official website after the signing of the meeting
minutes.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 69--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Commission sessions are considered valid only with a quorum of two thirds of members. The members
adopt decisions by open vote. A minimum three quarters majority is required for any resolution to take
effect.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 71--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Each granted scholarship is based on a transparent, merit based decision through this selection process.
It ensures highly selective outcomes, as annual applicant numbers reach approximately 10 000, but only
around 400–500 scholarships are granted. In 2013, 427 individuals were awarded the scholarship,
including Mr. Taximov. Thus, the acceptance rate typically remains near 4–5%, displaying the
program’s exclusivity and competitive standards.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 73--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Both CIP letters state that the Government of Kazakhstan, via CIP, serves as sponsor and guarantor 60
000 USD and covers the expenditures for the tuition fee, living costs (food and accommodation), round
trip travel, book allowance and medical examination for the academic year. As documented in the
record, the total scholarship funding allocated for the UCL academic year was approximately
100 000 USD. The other half (100 000 USD) of the overall award was used for 1.5 years of
preparatory courses prior to enrollment (language training, pre sessional course, and pre master
training).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 75--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov intended to pivot into Data Science and IT Project Management work. However, under the
Bolashak Scholarship the funded specialty abroad had to be related to the undergraduate degree,
therefore he undertook UCL’s MSc degree program (Building and Urban Design in Development). To
implement this interdisciplinary transition, in his MSc dissertation he used an IT method, the Spatial
Decision Support System (SDSS), for affordable housing needs assessment in Kazakhstan, with a
working prototype illustrated in his thesis.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 77--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The SDSS IT method included a data collection layer and a Java web crawler for collecting rental
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
advertisements from the main source, the krisha.kz website, and demographic statistics obtained from
the national portal stat.gov.kz. Moreover, datasets were stored in a MongoDB database. GIS
and base maps were used to prepare spatial boundaries, then displayed through the Google
Maps API. The final part of the thesis, user interface and presentations, which included
diagrams and page layout refinements, were prepared in graphic software such as AutoCAD and
CorelDRAW.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 79--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">This above mentioned thesis method allowed Mr. Taximov to sharpen his IT experience in a real world
project, ultimately serving as a bridge into IT Project Management.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 81--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Bolashak is a national, presidential scholarship awarded through competitive, expert reviewed selection
with final decisions by the Republican Commission chaired by the State Counselor and comprising
senior government officials appointed by the President. The three round selection process rigorously
evaluates Bolashak recipients, distinguishing them from the general applicant population with an
acceptance rate of approximately 4–5% in 2013. The CIP letters prove individual receipt by Mr.
Taximov and substantial value (total 200 000 USD). Although the funded master’s specialization was
focused not only on IT, Mr. Taximov’s MSc dissertation anchored his studies also in Building and
Information Modeling(BIM), information technologies and data systems, directly supporting his
subsequent career in IT Project Management. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38021r5">5<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BolashakFG_UCL --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38021r5">106<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BolashakFG_UCL --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38025r6">6<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BolashakFG_Embassy --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38025r6">109<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BolashakFG_Embassy --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38013r3">3<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:Decree2005 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38013r3">100<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:Decree2005 --></t4htlink>]

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.1.3    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-60002.1.3" name="x1-60002.1.3"></t4htlink>Letter of Appreciation for the SCO Summit. President of the Republic of Kazakhstan
(2024)</text:h> 

<!--l. 86--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In 2024, Kassym Jomart Tokayev, President of the Republic of Kazakhstan, awarded a formal
Presidential Letter of Appreciation to Mr. Taximov for his significant contribution to organizing and
conducting the Shanghai Cooperation Organization (SCO) Summit in Astana. The document bears
state insignia. From the Letter, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I express my gratitude for your active participation in preparing and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">holding the Shanghai Cooperation Organization summit in Astana at a high level.”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38033r8">8<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2024 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38033r8">115<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2024 --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 88--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Under Mr. Taximov’s leadership, the iKOMEK109 Monitoring and Rapid Response Center executed an
integrated operational program for the summit that combined organizational measures with citywide IT
infrastructure.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 91--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Organizational measures:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 94--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Managed 24/7 citizen request operations across public safety, housing, utilities, and other
      urban infrastructure through Next ITSM platform.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented digital monitoring of public channels. It continuously monitored mentions in
      social media, operator reports, resident signals and escalated incidents in real time.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Established a unified situational awareness center with reliable IT architecture. This facility
      integrated cross-agency workflows at iKOMEK109, orchestrating emergency and security
      services, to ensure timely response to minimize threats and critical incidents.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 99--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Use of IT infrastructure hardware and software complexes:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 102--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The city video surveillance complex (IP cameras, video walls, processing servers) monitored
      mass gathering sites, infrastructure facilities, rail and bus terminals, the airport and key
      roads and intersections.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Situational  video  analytics  supported  heat  maps,  crowding  detection  and  tracking  of
      pedestrian and vehicle flows.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Cyber protection measures included protected data channels (VPN and encryption), server
      and system redundancy and network activity monitoring to prevent unauthorized access.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >By integrating the system with public safety agencies (police, emergency and medical),
      automatic routing of alerts and instant interagency interaction were enabled.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 108--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The merger of these organizational workflows with surveillance analytics, cyber defense, and real time
digital communications provided a high level of safety for summit guests and participants, ensured
stable functioning of city infrastructure, and facilitated rapid response to threats in both physical and
digital domains.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 110--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Presidential commendation recognizes Mr. Taximov’s key role and leadership in applying IT tools
to address operations of national significance. The initiative required end to end ownership of mission
critical civic platforms, defining processes, orchestrating cross agency teams, integrating hardware and
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
software systems, instrumenting analytics, enforcing reliability and security controls, and operating at
international event scale. These are core responsibilities of project and program leadership in the IT
Project Management domain.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 112--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The “Letter of Appreciation of the President” is defined as an official form of state recognition under the
official Regulation on “Presidential Appreciation” (20 November 1996, <text:span 
text:style-name="tcrm-1200">№ </text:span>3230). The letter is awarded by
the Head of State for exceptional service and achievements benefiting society and the country. The
Regulation specifies that each Letter is personally signed by the President and bears national insignia.
The Regulation states that the award is formally registered by the Presidential Administration, and
entered into the official Registry of Presidential commendations. This established procedure confirms
that the Letter represents a formal governmental award rather than a ceremonial expression of
gratitude. Accordingly, a personally addressed and signed Presidential Letter of Appreciation constitutes
a nationally recognized distinction evidencing excellence and fulfills the evidentiary standard for a “lesser
nationally recognized prize or award for excellence in the field of endeavor”. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38033r8">8<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2024 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38033r8">115<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2024 --></t4htlink>]

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.1.4    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-70002.1.4" name="x1-70002.1.4"></t4htlink>Letter of Appreciation for the Extraordinary Presidential Election. President of the Republic of
Kazakhstan (2022)</text:h> 

<!--l. 119--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In November 2022, Kassym Jomart Tokayev, President of the Republic of Kazakhstan, awarded Mr.
Taximov a formal Presidential Letter of Appreciation for his significant contribution to the preparation
and conduct of the country’s extraordinary presidential election. From the letter, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I thank you for your</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">significant contribution to the preparation and conduct of the Presidential election of the Republic of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Kazakhstan.”</text:span></text:span>[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38029r7">7<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2022 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38029r7">112<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2022 --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 121--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">To ensure accuracy, transparency and security of the electoral process in the capital, Mr. Taximov led
an integrated program that combined organizational measures with a citywide technical implementation
based on the “Geonomics” Population Database platform.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 123--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Organizational measures:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 135--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 135--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Standardized voter list and automated polling station assignment by mapping Registration
      Address Codes (RAC), ensuring data integrity and algorithmic distribution of voters across
      polling stations.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Deployed  machine  learning  algorithms  and  custom  SQL  scripts  to  detect  anomalies
      in  residence  density  (&#x0022;rubber  apartments&#x0022;),  leveraging  interoperable  digital  tools  to
      synchronize corrective actions with district administrations and migration databases.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Managed the digital compilation of the final voter list using secure data pipelines, ensuring
      data consistency and seamless coordination with territorial commissions for final approval.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Architected a unified, IT-integrated election call center within iKOMEK109, implementing
      a  digitized  knowledge  base,  automated  frontend  interfaces,  and  algorithmic  escalation
      workflows for efficient citizen inquiry resolution.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Developed and launched high-availability digital services, including a Telegram bot API and
      web-based lookup tools, enabling voters to query polling station data quickly.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented real-time data analytics to monitor citizen inquiries throughout the election
      cycle, utilizing dashboard visualizations to identify trends and optimize support resources.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 137--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Technical architecture measures:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 140--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 141--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Provided basic platform functionality, use, and adaptation of the “Geonomics” Population
      Database information system.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Performed data integration and connection to the state database “Individuals” and other
      sources to update records, and enabled automatic linking of voters to polling stations by
      their registered address to eliminate manual errors.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented  GIS  visualization,  digital  mapping  of  polling  stations,  display  of  citizen
      distribution, territory analysis, and construction of polling station and district boundaries.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Corrected address geolocation and carried out reception and processing of vector, raster,
      and attribute data sets with the ability to edit and analyze in real time.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Ensured security and access, including authenticated access (login with electronic signature),
      secure export to approved formats (MDB, XLS), and service integration via REST, SOAP,
      and WSDL.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 149--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Geonomics program delivered highly accurate and up to date voter lists, transparent and
convenient citizen services (online tools and a unified call center) and a resilient, secure information
infrastructure for the national election. The program combined discovery (legal and stakeholder
requirements), delivery (data pipelines, GIS services, voter tools, contact center workflows) and
operations (security controls, SLAs, quality gates). It was an end to end lifecycle of a public sector
program at national scale.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 151--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">A Presidential Letter of Appreciation was conferred for the successful conduct of a countrywide election
constitutes a nationally recognized distinction evidencing excellence in a matter of national
importance. The “Letter of Appreciation of the President” is defined as an official form of state
recognition under the official Regulation on “Presidential Appreciation” (20 November 1996, <text:span 
text:style-name="tcrm-1200">№</text:span>
3230). The letter is awarded by the Head of State for exceptional service and achievements
benefiting society and the country. The Regulation specifies that each Letter is personally
signed by the President and bears national insignia. The Regulation states that the award is
formally registered by the Presidential Administration, and entered into the official Registry of
Presidential commendations. This established procedure confirms that the Letter represents a
formal governmental award rather than a ceremonial expression of gratitude. Accordingly, a
personally addressed and signed Presidential Letter of Appreciation constitutes a nationally
recognized distinction evidencing excellence and fulfills the evidentiary standard for a “lesser
nationally recognized prize or award for excellence in the field of endeavor”. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38029r7">7<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2022 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38029r7">112<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PresAlghys2022 --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 181--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Accordingly, a personally addressed, signed certificate of appreciation from an independent,
internationally recognized cybersecurity vendor such as Kaspersky constitutes a lesser internationally
recognized award for excellence and is probative of Mr. Taximov’s distinction in the field.

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.1.5    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-80002.1.5" name="x1-80002.1.5"></t4htlink>“Honorary Diploma” for the Presidential Election. Mayor of Astana (2022)</text:h> 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<!--l. 185--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Mayor of Astana city conferred an Honorary Diploma recognizing high professionalism and
organizational skills during the preparation and conduct of the 2022 extraordinary presidential election.
The commendation is signed and sealed. From the letter, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“For active involvement, high professionalism,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and for organizing and conducting the extraordinary Presidential election of the Republic of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Kazakhstan.”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38041r10">10<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimKurmet2022 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38041r10">121<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimKurmet2022 --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 187--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The diploma is awarded for Mr. Taximov’s citywide execution:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 190--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 191--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Technical  organization  and  updating  of  the  voter  database  (verification  and  automatic
      distribution of citizens to polling stations based on their registration address codes) using
      IT technologies.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Correction                        of                        overcrowded                        registration
      addresses in cooperation with district administrations and the migration service to ensure
      data accuracy.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Formation  and  coordination  of  voter  lists  with  district  administrations  and  territorial
      commissions.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Development of digital services (online polling station, analysis of voter requests) to support
      residents during elections.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Creation of a unified election call center in iKOMEK109 and training of operators and
      creation of a knowledge base.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 198--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Collectively, these systematic measures improved accuracy, transparency and citizen trust in the
electoral process. Owning the roadmap and delivery of mission critical civic products (voter data
services, contact center operations) across multiple agencies and constraints is a direct application of
product leadership. Although conferred by the Mayor of the capital city, the distinction honors work
performed for a national electoral event. It is widely recognized within the country and sector.
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38041r10">10<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimKurmet2022 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38041r10">121<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimKurmet2022 --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.1.6    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-90002.1.6" name="x1-90002.1.6"></t4htlink>Letter of Appreciation for the Day of Digitalization and IT Workers. Mayor of Astana
(2022)</text:h> 

<!--l. 202--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov received an official Letter of Appreciation from the Mayor of Astana for contributions to
the development of the city’s digital infrastructure and for the introduction of modern technologies into
city management (in honor of the Day of Digitalization and IT Workers). From the letter, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I sincerely</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">congratulate you on the Day of Digitalization and Information Technology Workers </text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">… I thank you for</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">your contribution to the development of our city’s information technology sector.”</text:span></text:span>[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38037r9">9<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimAlgys2022 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38037r9">118<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimAlgys2022 --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 204--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">As a Head-IT Project Manager of iKOMEK109 in 2022, Mr. Taximov led:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 207--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 208--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Expansion of channels for digital feedback by citizens (mobile app, Telegram bots, social
      networks), allowing 24/7 requests for utilities, technical maintenance, and public safety.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Strengthening the information security system in the contact center and online services,
      protecting personal data, and ensuring continuity of service.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Automating request processing, transitioning from a traditional call center to an analytical
      intelligent platform, increasing speed and transparency.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Development of dashboards and analytics to support City Hall’s management of incident
      response and infrastructure planning.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 214--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">These improvements increased the reliability of city infrastructure and strengthened Astana’s position as
a regional leader in digitalization. The outcomes reflect project leadership, multi channel UX, backlog
and roadmap control, security and reliability requirements, KPI driven responsiveness and
stakeholder alignment at the city executive level. The formal commendation was issued by
the Mayor of the capital, and it is recognized as a national government award. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38037r9">9<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimAlgys2022 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38037r9">118<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AkimAlgys2022 --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-100002.2" name="x1-100002.2"></t4htlink>Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s membership in associations in the field that require outstanding
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
achievement of their members</text:h> 


<!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.2.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-110002.2.1" name="x1-110002.2.1"></t4htlink>Kazakhstan Information Security Association</text:h> 

<!--l. 6--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The membership of Mr. Taximov is confirmed by the signed admission decision of July 1, 2025, with
outgoing No. 010725 2. The decision bears the seal of the Association and the signature of the Chair,
Mr. Viktor Pokusov. From the letter, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Approve and include Askar Taximov as a member of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">community of information security and information technology professionals.”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38045r11">11<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaibAdmissionLetter --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38045r11">124<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaibAdmissionLetter --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 8--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The record and independent materials describe a national professional association in information
security and information technology. It operates across Kazakhstan and unites organizations that work
directly in digital systems and security. It is stated in the letter that, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“The Association unites thirty</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">organizations in the Republic of Kazakhstan including competence centers, testing laboratories,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">manufacturers of information protection tools, universities, research bodies and major operators of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">personal data.”</text:span></text:span> KISA Admission Decision (English translation).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 10--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The admission decision is on association letterhead and shows the date, signature, seal and outgoing
number on the face of the record. It states that membership is granted for work, significant experience
and professional achievements in information technology, cybersecurity and project management. It also
lists objective prerequisites and confirms that admission is not automatic and is not based on payment
of dues [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38045r11">11<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaibAdmissionLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38045r11">124<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaibAdmissionLetter --></t4htlink>]. They include
</text:p> 
<!--l. 13--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 14--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Advanced   technical   education   confirming   expertise   in   IT,   cybersecurity,   systems
      architecture, digitalization and innovation.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >More than 10 years of professional and research experience, with at least 5 years in IT
      leadership positions.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >International project management certifications (including Product Owner and Product
      Manager) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38065r16">16<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PMCertificate --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38065r16">143<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PMCertificate --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Successful completion of advanced qualification examinations such as Program Increment
      (PI) Planning, Leadership for PI Planning, Iteration Execution and PI Execution.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Written recommendations from recognized experts in IT and digitalization, confirming an
      impeccable professional reputation.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Authorship of original and effective developments and methodologies in IT, innovation and
      technology transfer.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Presentations delivered at national and international conferences.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 23--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The level of achievement follows from the multifactor prerequisites, the documented record and the
expert review that leads to selective admission.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 25--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The letter says, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“A candidate is admitted by the decision of the Association Council. The Council</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">consists of leading professional experts in information technology and cybersecurity, certified information</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">security officers and project managers of national and international level.”</text:span></text:span> KISA Admission Decision
(English translation) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38045r11">11<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaibAdmissionLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38045r11">124<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaibAdmissionLetter --></t4htlink>]. The record identifies the decision makers by name and
title as shown in the decision and on the association roster, such as the Chair, Viktor Pokusov, and
council members who hold national leadership roles in cybersecurity and IT [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38049r12">12<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KISASite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38049r12">127<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KISASite --></t4htlink>].
This shows that applicants are evaluated by recognized experts consistent with the regulatory standard
for expert evaluation.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 27--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">An official entry on the national portal Career.enbek.kz shows accreditation by the National Chamber of
Entrepreneurs “Atameken” as a Center for Recognition of Professional Qualifications in information
security and in information and communication technologies. As stated in the letter, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Functions include</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development of professional standards, standardized competency assessments with employer</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">participation and certification of qualifications in core specialties of information security</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and information and communication technologies.”</text:span></text:span> Career.enbek.kz registry entry (English
translation) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38069r17">17<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:CareerKISA --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38069r17">146<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:CareerKISA --></t4htlink>]. This confirms an expert evaluation function in the same
field.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 29--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Publicly available materials also describe the following activities related to the establishment and
national activities:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 32--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 33--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Established  in  August  2017  with  the  aim  of  consolidating  scientific,  industrial,  and
      government  expertise  to  implement  national  priorities  in  the  field  of  security  and
      informatization [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38049r12">12<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KISASite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38049r12">127<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KISASite --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >University and industry councils on education and staffing in the field of cybersecurity
      [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38053r13">13<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KISAMeeting --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38053r13">130<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KISAMeeting --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Public speeches by Chairman Viktor Pokusov on policy and security issues [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38057r14">14<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PokusovTalk --></t4htlink>,
      page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38057r14">135<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PokusovTalk --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >National round tables and consultative events in Astana [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38061r15">15<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:RoundTable --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38061r15">138<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:RoundTable --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 39--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The record shows a professional association in information security and information technology.
Membership is conditioned on objective achievements that include education, leadership, certifications,
methods and public speaking. The selection is made by recognized experts who serve on the
Association Council. There is independent national accreditation for qualification recognition and
competency assessment. Accordingly, the record satisfies the membership criterion for associations
that admit members on the basis of outstanding achievements, as evaluated by recognized
experts.
</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.3    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-120002.3" name="x1-120002.3"></t4htlink>Published material about Mr. Taximov in professional or major media relating to his
work</text:h> 

<!--l. 5--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">One of the key indicators of extraordinary ability is the publication of material about the individual’s
work in professional, major trade publications, or other major media outlets. Mr. Taximov’s work in IT
Project Management has garnered substantial recognition in both industry and media, demonstrating
the impact and significance of his contributions. Below are some examples of such published
material:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 14--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 16--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Kazakhstanskaya Pravda</text:span></text:span></text:span> is a national newspaper that has been published since 1920
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      and is distributed throughout the country. The newspaper’s historical circulation ranges
      from 80 000 to 110 000 copies each year, and it has offices in cities throughout the country.
      It also received state honors including the Order of the Red Banner of Labour in 1958. The
      newspaper has active digital channels its Instagram account has around 160 000 followers
      and an online portal with a wide national audience. These factors allow it to be classified as
      a major media outlet in Kazakhstan. This national newspaper article presents iKOMEK109
      under Mr. Taximov’s leadership as a 24/7 digital response and analytics ecosystem. It
      highlights integration with more than 12000 Sergek cameras, lists the breadth of connected
      agencies,  and  notes  omnichannel  intake  and  analytics  used  to  surface  risks.  The  piece
      references Mr. Taximov and his work, academic background, more than ten publications, the
      creation of iKOMEK 2.0 and NextITSM, the Life Signal geolocation service with Google and
      Apple, and GIS and SDSS research for planning. It also quotes him directly and describes
      results, systems, projects, and research with operational metrics.
      </text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >&#x0022;Urban   governance   digitalization&#x0022;   <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Kazakhstanskaya  Pravda</text:span></text:span>,   18   July   2025,   Asya
      Petrova. URL <t4htlink 
href="https://kazpravda.kz/n/tsifrovizatsiya-v-gorodskom-upravlenii/" class="url" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ectt-1200">https://kazpravda.kz/n/tsifrovizatsiya-v-gorodskom-upravlenii/</text:span></t4htlink>
      </text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The outlet holds a print and online newspaper registration under primary certificate <text:span 
text:style-name="tcrm-1200">№</text:span>
      16029-SI, issued on 9 June 2016. Its web edition at www.kazpravda.kz was subsequently
      re-registered  under  certificate  <text:span 
text:style-name="tcrm-1200">№  </text:span>KZ48VPY00062700,  issued  on  12  January  2023  by
