<!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.4    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4" name="x1-130002.4"></t4htlink>Evidence that Mr. Taximov has been asked to judge the work of others in the same or an allied
field</text:h> 


<!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-140002.4.1" name="x1-140002.4.1"></t4htlink>Astana International University (AIU) - Permanent independent peer reviewer of the university
journal</text:h> 

<!--l. 247--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The President of Astana International University confirms on institutional letterhead that Mr. Taximov
is a permanent independent reviewer of the scientific journal of our university <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“International Science</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Reviews. Natural Sciences and Technologies series”</text:span></text:span>. The letter specifies that, considering Mr. Taximov’s
expertise in IT and innovation, he <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“considers and evaluates scientific works and articles in innovative</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and information technology areas”</text:span></text:span> including topics such as <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“use of Big Data in managing national</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">companies, introduction of information technologies in startup projects, creation of technologies for data</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">analysis in social projects, use of artificial intelligence in engineering systems and the use of Data</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Science when forming information security”</text:span></text:span> (English translation of the official letter) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38129r32">32<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUReviewer --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38129r32">196<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUReviewer --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 249--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The same AIU letter describes the substantive peer review functions performed by Mr. Taximov.
He <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“assesses the relevance of the topic studied, the authenticity of the presented facts, the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">argumentation and clarity of the author’s exposition and conclusions”</text:span></text:span> and, crucially, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“formulates a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">decision on the admission of the article, the possibility or impossibility of publication in the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">above mentioned journal or the need for further revision”</text:span></text:span> (English translation) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38129r32">32<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUReviewer --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38129r32">196<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUReviewer --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 251--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">These statements prove actual participation with publish, revise, and decline outcomes, as required by
USCIS. AIUs journal portal identifies the reviewed venue as <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">(International Science Reviews. Natural</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Sciences and Technologies Series)</text:span></text:span> with ISSN 2707 4862 and owned by ‘Astana International University’
LLP (Astana, Kazakhstan). Its thematic focus is explicitly <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“devoted to research in the field of natural</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">sciences </text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">…</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> as well as technologies such as information technology, information security, engineering,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">metallurgy and oil and gas production and processing”</text:span></text:span> and the periodicity is <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“4 times a year”</text:span></text:span>
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38133r33">33<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUScienceSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38133r33">199<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUScienceSite --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 253--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Due to the fact that the journals scope expressly includes information technology and information
security the works judged are in the same or allied field to IT Project Management. AIUs own overview
states the university’s mission is <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“to provide a high level of knowledge and competence </text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">…</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> through</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">academic excellence, research and innovation to serve the nation and the world”</text:span></text:span> and its vision is
to be <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“a modern global university generating and disseminating knowledge, research and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">innovation for the Eurasian space.”</text:span></text:span> Among listed priorities are <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">conducting fundamental and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">applied research and training in information and communication technologies</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38137r34">34<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUSite --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38137r34">203<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUSite --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 255--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Public profiles and institutional pages confirm the university’s academic activity:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 258--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The official Instagram profile confirms AIU operates as a higher education institution in
      Astana [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38141r35">35<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUInstagram --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38141r35">207<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUInstagram --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The university’s website outlines its mission to provide knowledge through research and
      innovation [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38137r34">34<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38137r34">203<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUSite --></t4htlink>].
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The  journal  portal  lists  ISSN  2707  4862  and  confirms  the  scope  covers  information
      technology and security [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38133r33">33<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUScienceSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38133r33">199<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUScienceSite --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 262--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">These sources prove the judging occurred in a recognized scholarly venue [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38141r35">35<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUInstagram --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38141r35">207<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUInstagram --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38137r34">34<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38137r34">203<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUSite --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38133r33">33<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUScienceSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38133r33">199<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AIUScienceSite --></t4htlink>].

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-150002.4.2" name="x1-150002.4.2"></t4htlink>L.N. Gumilyov Eurasian National University (ENU) - Permanent reviewer of the university
journal <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">”Vestnik ENU”</text:span></text:span></text:h> 

<!--l. 269--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Department of Science and Commercialization of L.N. Gumilyov Eurasian National University
confirms that Mr. Taximov <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“is indeed a reviewer of the scientific journal ‘Vestnik of L.N. Gumilyov</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Eurasian National University’ and on a permanent basis participates in the evaluation of scientific</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">articles”</text:span></text:span> on topics including <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“the introduction of information and innovative technologies in companies,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">trends in IT technologies and their effective influence on regional development, Data Science as an</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">instrument to increase business profitability, SQL and Data analytics”</text:span></text:span> (English translation of the official
letter) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38145r36">36<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUReviewer --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38145r36">210<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUReviewer --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 271--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">ENU specifies that Mr. Taximov reviews submissions for <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“scientific novelty, the relevance of the problem,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">scientific and practical significance of the research, depth of elaboration of the topic, style of presentation</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and innovative approach to the scientific work”</text:span></text:span> and, based on that assessment, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“makes a conclusion on</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the advisability of publishing the article or the need for rejection or revision”</text:span></text:span> (English translation)
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38145r36">36<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUReviewer --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38145r36">210<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUReviewer --></t4htlink>]. This demonstrates that Mr. Taximov actually judged manuscripts and issued
accept revise reject decisions.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 273--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">ENU describes a research ecosystem with over 160 scientific projects. These include mathematical
modeling and high technologies [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38149r37">37<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUScienceSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38149r37">213<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUScienceSite --></t4htlink>]. The university holds special status and
international recognition [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38153r38">38<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38153r38">217<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUSite --></t4htlink>]. Mr. Taximov reviewed Data Science and IT trends
here. This work aligns with IT Project Management. Public sources confirm ENU’s standing:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 276--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The  verified  Instagram  profile  corroborates  the  university’s  identity  and  visibility
      [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38161r40">40<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUInstagram --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38161r40">226<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUInstagram --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Official  pages  detail  research  centers,  laboratories,  and  international  accreditations
      [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38153r38">38<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38153r38">217<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUSite --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38149r37">37<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUScienceSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38149r37">213<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUScienceSite --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >QS  World  University  Rankings  place  ENU  high  in  Central  Asia.  This  validates  the
      university’s reputation [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38157r39">39<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUQSRanking --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38157r39">222<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUQSRanking --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 280--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">These sources confirm ENU is a recognized scholarly venue, and thatMr. Taximov was a permanent
reviewer of the scientific journal ‘Vestnik’[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38153r38">38<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38153r38">217<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUSite --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38149r37">37<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUScienceSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38149r37">213<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUScienceSite --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38157r39">39<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUQSRanking --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38157r39">222<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUQSRanking --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38161r40">40<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUInstagram --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38161r40">226<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ENUInstagram --></t4htlink>].

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.3    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-160002.4.3" name="x1-160002.4.3"></t4htlink>Public Foundation “ITeachMe” - Independent Expert and Jury Member (OrleTECH
finals)</text:h> 

<!--l. 287--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Public Foundation “ITeachMe” (Center for Competence Development) is a national nonprofit
organization in Kazakhstan dedicated to developing digital skills, creativity, and employability, with a
strong emphasis on inclusion. Its programs are designed to support socially vulnerable groups, including
persons with disabilities, by offering training in Kazakh, Russian, and sign language, as well as
dedicated inclusive educational tracks. Through flagship initiatives such as OrleTECH, the foundation
partners with major stakeholders, including Samruk Kazyna Trust, Shell Kazakhstan, and leading
technology platforms.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 289--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The OrleTECH curriculum combines a three stage national competition, an offline Soft Skills
camp, three months of intensive online Hard Skills training, and a final diploma defense
before a professional jury, followed by a public awards ceremony. The foundation reports
strong outcomes, including a 90 percent employment rate among participants, more than
180 graduates, over 80 Soft Skills camp participants, and cooperation with more than 40
employer partners. This institutional profile confirms that jury service at OrleTECH is a
professional, selective, and nationally visible activity directly aligned with the IT and AI
field.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 291--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Public Foundation “ITeachMe” formally invited Mr. Taximov to serve as an honorary jury
member for the OrleTECH finals and awards ceremony. The 2024 invitation states (English
translation):
</text:p> 
<!--l. 292--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“We invite you to participate in the awards ceremony for OrleTECH graduates and also invite</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">you to act as an honorary member of the jury during the defense of students’ course projects.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">The defense and ceremony will take place on 28 November 2024 at the Wyndham Garden Astana</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">conference hall ‘Altai’.” [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">42</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">232</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 296--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In the 2023 invitation also asked Mr. Taximov <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“to take part in the final of the seventh season and to</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">become an honorary member of the jury,”</text:span></text:span> with the venue and date specified as Astana Hub on 02
November 2023 at 16:30 [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">41<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">229<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 298--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The official agendas document the structure of the jury reviewed defenses across specific tracks. For
2023, course project defenses before the jury were organized by rooms dedicated to UI/UX Design,
Motion Design, SMM and copywriting, Mobile videography, and Graphic design, followed by formal
awards blocks. For 2024, the program explicitly listed three judged defenses, NoCode, UX/UI plus Web
Master, and AI Specialist, together with the presentation of jury members and a formal jury meeting
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">41<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">229<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42">42<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42">232<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 300--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Within these events, Mr. Taximov’s role as a jury member consisted of participating in live defense
sessions, evaluating students’ course projects against professional and industry standards, and
contributing to collective jury deliberations and final assessments. Beyond the formal invitations and
programs, photographic and social media records document Mr. Taximov’s presence in the jury room
during live defenses, further confirming his active participation in the evaluation process [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38173r43">43<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OrleJudgingInsta --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38173r43">235<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OrleJudgingInsta --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38177r44">44<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OrleJudgingPhoto --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38177r44">239<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OrleJudgingPhoto --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38193r48">48<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMe2024Photo --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38193r48">261<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMe2024Photo --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 302--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The judged tracks NoCode, UX/UI plus Web, and AI Specialist are squarely within the domains of
computer science, information technology, and applied artificial intelligence. The 2023 tracks likewise
covered core digital disciplines, including UI/UX design, Motion Design, SMM and copywriting, Mobile
videography, and Graphic design, all of which were evaluated by the professional jury [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">41<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">229<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42">42<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42">232<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 304--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The invitations also describe a multi stage national selection and graduation pipeline. For OrleTECH
2024, more than 1,800 applications were submitted, with 232 students selected after a three
stage competition. Following approximately 3.5 months of training, more than 120 graduates
completed and presented their projects online, with 50 finalists traveling to Astana for the offline
defense before the jury. The 2023 invitation similarly notes more than one and a half thousand
applications, with approximately 150 students passing the selection process and completing four
months of instruction prior to the jury reviewed final [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42">42<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38169r42">232<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInvitation2024 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">41<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38165r41">229<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeInv2023 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 306--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The OrleTECH program materials further describe the three main educational tracks: NoCode, focused
on building websites and applications without coding; UX/UI Design plus Web, emphasizing usable and
visually engaging digital products; and AI Specialist, centered on applying artificial intelligence to create
texts, images, animations, and video content. Program materials also present cumulative results,
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
including high employment outcomes, extensive Soft Skills training participation, and broad employer
engagement [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38181r45">45<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OrleTechSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38181r45">250<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OrleTechSite --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 308--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Finally, the foundation’s certificate confirms that Mr. Taximov has served on an ongoing basis since
November 2022 as an external expert, jury member, and consultant for multiple program finals,
including ITeachMe 6.0, ITeachMe 7.0, and OrleTECH 2.0. His responsibilities included independent
professional evaluation of projects across UI UX design, graphic and motion design, SMM, copywriting,
mobile videography, No-code development, and AI applications, as well as the preparation of expert
recommendations and advisory support in the areas of digital transformation and information security
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38185r46">46<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeCertificate --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38185r46">255<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ITeachMeCertificate --></t4htlink>].

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.4    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-170002.4.4" name="x1-170002.4.4"></t4htlink>Kaspersky Lab KZ Expert commission on IT, Data Protection and Cybersecurity</text:h> 

<!--l. 315--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kaspersky is a globally recognized cybersecurity company founded in 1997, providing security
technologies for consumers and enterprises worldwide. Independent industry testing organizations
consistently document Kaspersky’s high status in the cybersecurity market. AV TEST reports that
Kaspersky received nine awards during its 2024 awards cycle, reflecting strong protection, performance,
and usability results across multiple product categories. SE Labs enterprise endpoint security testing
likewise places Kaspersky among the strongest performers, demonstrating effective threat prevention
while allowing legitimate applications to operate without disruption. These independent evaluations
confirm Kaspersky’s position as a top tier authority in global cybersecurity [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38265r66">66<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVTest2024 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38265r66">340<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVTest2024 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38269r67">67<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVComparatives --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38269r67">345<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVComparatives --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 317--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">On official corporate letterhead, Kaspersky Lab (Kazakhstan) confirms that Mr. Taximov, since
September 2019 to the present, has been engaged on a permanent basis as a leading expert and
consultant participating in an expert commission responsible for the development, evaluation,
and analysis of business projects in information technology and data security, including
infrastructure digitalization projects and cybersecurity. This confirmation is provided in English
translation in the official correspondence issued by Kaspersky Lab (Kazakhstan) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38197r49">49<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyExpert --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38197r49">272<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyExpert --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 319--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The same letter details that within this expert role Mr. Taximov performs the following functions:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 322--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >researches and analyzes global trends in municipal service digitalization using data analytics
      tools;
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >analyzes projects related to cybersecurity, data protection, and cloud solutions;
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >conducts information technology expert review of business projects to assess feasibility and
      applicability based on available tools and resources;
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >provides expert conclusions with comments and clarifications on reviewed initiatives and
      proposes ideas and development directions for improvement.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 327--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">These responsibilities demonstrate substantive judging activity, including structured expert review,
written evaluations, and professional conclusions that guide whether projects should be approved,
revised, optimized, or rejected [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38197r49">49<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyExpert --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38197r49">272<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyExpert --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 329--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">All subject areas reviewed by the expert commission, including enterprise IT projects, data protection
systems, cloud solutions, cybersecurity initiatives, and analytics driven digitalization, fall directly within
Mr. Taximov’s field of IT Project Management. The commission operates within a major international
cybersecurity vendor, and the evaluated works consist of business critical IT security projects and
infrastructure digitalization initiatives. The requirement to prepare formal expert conclusions and
propose technical and strategic improvements confirms that Mr. Taximov judges the work of
professional engineering and project teams against established technical, security, and operational
standards.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 331--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The confirmation letter bears Kaspersky’s official corporate letterhead, including the Kazakhstan office
address, corporate contact details, institutional seal, and the Managing Director’s signature, providing
direct points of verification. Independent third party evaluations from AV TEST and SE
Labs, together with international media reporting, further substantiate Kaspersky’s role as a
distinguished and globally recognized authority in cybersecurity. In this context, Mr. Taximov’s long
term service as a permanent expert consultant on Kaspersky’s expert commission represents
judging activity of high professional significance within the same allied field [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38197r49">49<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyExpert --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38197r49">272<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyExpert --></t4htlink>].

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.5    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-180002.4.5" name="x1-180002.4.5"></t4htlink>iKOMEK109 (Governance of Astana) - Permanent member of the Commission on Digital
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
Development</text:h> 

<!--l. 338--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The City Center of Monitoring and Rapid Response of the Governance of Astana (iKOMEK109 )
confirms on official letterhead that Mr. Taximov has served since September 2022 as a permanent
member of the Commission on Digital Development and the Use of Information Technologies performing
expert activities focused on the analysis, evaluation and development of digital initiatives [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38201r50">50<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IkomekCommission --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38201r50">275<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IkomekCommission --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 340--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The same letter specifies the judging work Mr. Taximov performs and the outcomes of his reviews:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 343--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Evaluation and expert review of digital initiatives.</text:span></text:span> Reviews digital-transformation
      proposals, checks feasibility and expected business value, and assesses risks of implementing
      new solutions. Provides an expert conclusion on whether initiatives should be approved,
      revised, or rejected.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Internal policies and governance for IT implementation.</text:span></text:span> Analyzes and updates
      internal  rules,  policies,  and  guidelines  that  govern  technology  deployment.  Reviews
      how  relevant  legal  requirements  and  international  practices  apply  to  the  company  and
      recommends practical improvements to keep processes compliant and workable.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Implementation oversight and performance control.</text:span></text:span> Monitors delivery of approved
      IT projects, reviews KPI results, and identifies gaps. Prepares recommendations to optimize
      performance and improve impact on business processes.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Information   security   and   data   protection.</text:span></text:span>  Assesses   whether   proposed   and
      implemented solutions meet cybersecurity and personal-data requirements. Identifies key
      risks in data processing and storage and recommends concrete safeguards (for example,
      stronger access control, encryption, and monitoring).
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Technology scouting and strategic recommendations.</text:span></text:span> Tracks emerging technologies
      (AI, big data, automation, digital platforms), evaluates where they can realistically improve
      operations,  and  recommends  the  most  promising  options  aligned  with  the  company’s
      priorities.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 350--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Based on these evaluations Mr. Taximov forms recommendations on adoption approval, coordination,
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
revision or refusal of the reviewed documents and initiatives issuing written conclusions where
inconsistencies are found [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38201r50">50<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IkomekCommission --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38201r50">275<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IkomekCommission --></t4htlink>]. All reviewed matters enterprise IT, digital platforms,
AI big data initiatives, automation and information security compliance ZTA, ISO 27001, GDPR, NIST
belong to Mr. Taximov’s field of IT Project Management satisfying USCISs same or allied field
requirement.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 352--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">iKOMEK109 functions as the city’s 24/7 monitoring center. The official site lists city metrics and the
administration roster [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38221r55">55<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38221r55">291<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekSiteShot --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 354--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Public evidence confirms its scale:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 357--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The government portal identifies iKOMEK109 as the single contact point. It offers over
      2,500 services and resolves most requests immediately [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38213r53">53<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekGov --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38213r53">285<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekGov --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >A Senate press release reports that Senate Deputy Andrey Lukin visited iKOMEK109 and
      highlights its performance in 2025, including that over 90% of requests were reviewed on
      time [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38233r58">58<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekSenate --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38233r58">306<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekSenate --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The verified Instagram profile displays over 230 000 followers. This confirms its public
      prominence [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38217r54">54<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekInstagramShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38217r54">288<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 


<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.6    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-190002.4.6" name="x1-190002.4.6"></t4htlink>JSC “State Technical Service” (STS) - Expert commission on information security and
digitalization</text:h> 

<!--l. 369--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">JSC “State Technical Service” certifies on official letterhead (seal and signature) that since January 2022
Mr. Taximov has been engaged on a permanent basis as (i) an external expert on technology transfer,
information security and digitalization and (ii) an Independent Director Board member. He takes part
as a lead expert analyst in the expert commission evaluating the information security posture of e
government informatization facilities to identify threats incidents and ensure secure operation and data
protection [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38205r51">51<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSCommission --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38205r51">279<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSCommission --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 371--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The STS certificate details concrete judging work and outcomes including:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 374--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Expert review of submissions on IS posture of e government facilities analysis of incidents
      threats with mitigation and data protection recommendations.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Line by line review of draft normative legal acts on information security, digitalization and
      AI at informatization objects written expert comments and conclusions.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Independent Director oversight of technical projects business process design for trials of the
      Synaq portal pilot testing of the National video monitoring system data collection processing
      design for CyberDigest review of an IP address packet filtering module.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Issuance of formal expert opinions recommending adoption, revision or rejection of reviewed
      projects normative acts [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38205r51">51<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSCommission --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38205r51">279<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSCommission --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 380--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">All judged matters information security architectures and controls, cybersecurity compliance, AI use
within state informatization systems and national digital platforms are within Mr. Taximov’s field of IT
Project Management.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 382--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">STS is formally recognized as the technological core of Kazakhstans cyber shield Its official public pages
describe mission and monopoly functions including Unified Internet e mail gateways for e
government testing informatization facilities for IS compliance coordination monitoring of
incidents operation of the National Video Monitoring System SOC functions and national
certification authority [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38237r59">59<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38237r59">310<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSSiteShot --></t4htlink>]. Independent corroboration includes the following:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 385--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >STS official website (English and About pages) provides mission statements national scale
      statistics (blocked attacks, DDOS mitigation) and partner logos confirming its status as the
      state designated cyber defense operator [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38237r59">59<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38237r59">310<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSSiteShot --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >STS verified Instagram profile shows public facing communication as a national enterprise
      corroborating STSs visibility and reputation [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38241r60">60<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSInstagramShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38241r60">316<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 


                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.4.7    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-200002.4.7" name="x1-200002.4.7"></t4htlink>Elorda Qurylys Kompaniyasy (EQK) - Enterprise expert commissions</text:h> 

<!--l. 394--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Elorda Qurylys Kompaniyasy (EQK) confirms that since March 15, 2022 Mr. Taximov has been engaged
on an ongoing basis as an expert in information technologies and innovation to review matters
and projects related to the introduction and development of these areas in the company
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38209r52">52<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKExpert --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38209r52">282<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKExpert --></t4htlink>]. The letter, signed by the General Director specifies that Mr. Taximov:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 397--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >analyzes technological solutions proposed for optimization of construction processes and
      asset management;
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >evaluates  innovative  technologies  to  increase  the  efficiency  and  quality  of  construction
      projects;
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >conducts detailed research of automation digitalization projects to determine applicability
      for each site;
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >analyzes risks and opportunities related to introducing IT solutions in civil construction;
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >consults  on  integration  of  innovative  systems  and  technologies  into  existing  business
      processes.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 404--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Based on the above Mr. Taximov prepares analytical reports and expert conclusions on feasibility and
implementation for each matter considered [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38209r52">52<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKExpert --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38209r52">282<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKExpert --></t4htlink>]. The judging concerns enterprise
digitalization, automation and integration of IT solutions squarely within Mr. Taximov’s field of IT
Project Management.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 406--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">EQK is a municipal developer tasked with completing shared equity housing projects in Astana. Its
public footprint substantiates its scale and credibility:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 409--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Official  EQK  website  details  the  companys  mission,  mandate  to  resolve  shared  equity
      housing, delivered residential complexes and project portfolio [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38245r61">61<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38245r61">319<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKSiteShot --></t4htlink>].
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Verified   Instagram   profile   shows   nearly   470   posts   (2025)   demonstrating   active
      communication with the public and transparency about delivering 141 buildings for 15,500+
      families [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38249r62">62<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKInstagramShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38249r62">324<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 


<!--end of subsubsection--><!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.5    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5" name="x1-210002.5"></t4htlink>Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s original scientific and business related contributions of major
significance to the field</text:h> 


<!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.5.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-220002.5.1" name="x1-220002.5.1"></t4htlink>National IT infrastructure and cybersecurity</text:h> 

<!--l. 178--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov managed large scale IT and cybersecurity projects affecting banks, ministries and national
e-government systems.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 181--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Askar Zhunisbek. Chairman of the Management Board, JSC “State Technical Service” (STS)</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 183--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Askar Zhunisbek characterizes Mr. Taximov not only as a contributor to internal operations, but as a
nationally consequential cybersecurity and digitalization professional. In his recommendation letter, he
describes Mr. Taximov as <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“an outstanding professional in the field of information technologies and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">innovative developments, whose activity has left a significant mark in the development of digitalization</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and security of our country. Over the past six years, Askar Taximov held leadership positions in various</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">quasi-public companies, where he proved himself as a true leader and innovator. Thanks to his initiatives</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and professionalism, significant projects were implemented aimed at introducing advanced</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">technologies and improving infrastructure in the areas of technology transfer, digitalization, smart</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">cities, cybersecurity, and others... his deep understanding of the specifics of the industry,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">as well as the ability to apply the latest solutions, made it possible to achieve impressive</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">results.”</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 185--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek places Mr. Taximov’s work in the context of critical infrastructure compliance systems,
stating:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 186--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Mr. Taximov participated in the development of the Synaq Internet portal, implemented to</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">automate the process of providing the service of testing ‘electronic government’ informatization</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">objects and information systems classified as critical objects of the information and communication</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">infrastructure, for compliance with information security requirements”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 189--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">This project is of national strategic importance, as it serves as the primary security shield for
Kazakhstan’s critical digital infrastructure and protects the sensitive data of millions of
citizens.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 191--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek further describes Mr. Taximov’s contribution to Internet-scale vulnerability discovery
supporting national cyber defense workflows:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 192--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As part of cross-sector coordination on monitoring information security, protection, and the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">secure functioning of the Kazakhstan segment of the Internet, in 2023 JSC ‘STS’ carried out</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">work on the development of a search system for collecting information on the security level</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of devices connected to the Internet ScanKZ, at the scale of the Kazakhstan segment of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Internet. Mr. Taximov played a key role in the development of components of this system. As</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">a result of the development of ScanKZ, the following was achieved: improvement of KZ-CERT’s</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">current activities for preventing computer security threats through the automatic identification of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">vulnerable objects on the network,” and “expansion of the ability to assess the security posture of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">devices in Kazakhstan and worldwide connected to the Internet”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 196--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In addition, Zhunisbek emphasizes long-term industry impact:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 197--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Mr. Taximov’s contribution to digitalization and the development of innovative technologies</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">had a long-term effect on the industry</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">…Thanks to his efforts, it was possible to accelerate packet</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">processing with a customized router based on Data Plane Development Kit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">…he optimized the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">operation of routing and load balancing modules, which made it possible to significantly reduce</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">delays in data transmission and increase the speed of processing network traffic of central servers</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">supporting the information security system. This contribution was highly appreciated by colleagues</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and partners, and also received recognition at the state level”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 201--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek concludes by directly summarizing the broader significance of Mr. Taximov’s work,
stating: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Mr. Taximov is a professional of the highest level, whose work makes a significant</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">contribution to the development of information technologies and innovations.”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38273r68">68<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSContribution --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38273r68">348<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSContribution --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 205--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Aidos Tokayev. Information Security Officer, City Monitoring and Rapid Response Center,</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span text:style-name="underline" >Administration of Astana</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 208--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Aidos Tokayev states that Mr. Taximov’s work made a substantial contribution to strengthening
Kazakhstan’s national digital infrastructure and cybersecurity, particularly through large-scale
e-government gateway modernization, high-performance security prototypes, and operational
vulnerability-scanning capabilities for government systems.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 210--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">About the <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Project ‘Maintenance of the unified Internet access gateway and the unified email gateway of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the ‘electronic government’ of the Republic of Kazakhstan”</text:span></text:span> he states that:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 211--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Development of an AI-based content filtering module that allows real-time analysis of Internet</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">traffic and blocking of potential threats. Implementation of a dynamic traffic routing methodology,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">which increased the gateway performance by 23% and reduced the system response time by 17%. As</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">a result of the project, the system fault tolerance increased, cyber threats decreased, and operating</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">costs were optimized by 157.2 million tenge per year”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 215--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Tokayev further highlights Mr. Taximov’s leadership in project <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Development of prototypes of software</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">products for information security”</text:span></text:span>, resulting in measurable improvements in speed, latency, and budget
efficiency:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 216--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In  particular,  he  led  an  initiative  to  optimize  DPDK  traffic  and  implement  solutions  that</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">increased the speed of network traffic processing by 34%. The implementation of these solutions</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">ensured a 40% increase in the throughput of the network infrastructure and optimization of capital</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">expenditures by 104.16 million tenge”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 220--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He also underscores Mr. Taximov’s role in project <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Development of a prototype module ‘Vulnerability</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Scanner”’</text:span></text:span>, noting:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 221--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Within this project, scripts for automatic detection of 20 types of vulnerabilities were developed, which</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">made it possible to significantly increase the level of cyber protection of government information systems.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Thanks to Askar’s impressive work, significant results have been achieved in the areas of information</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">security, digital monitoring, and data management. His contribution to the development of the national</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">IT infrastructure cannot be overstated:</text:span>
     </text:p> 
<!--l. 224--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

     <text:list-item>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">A 31% reduction in the number of failures in government IT systems.</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Optimization  of  government  operating  costs  through  the  implementation  of  innovative</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">solutions.”</text:span></text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 229--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Summarizing his assessment, Mr. Tokayev provides a broader evaluation of Mr. Taximov’s professional
significance and long-term impact: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Summarizing the above, I would like to emphasize that this specialist</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">has not only made a significant contribution to the development of the IT industry, information security,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and cybersecurity, but continues to actively shape the future directions of this field. His leadership</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">qualities, strategic thinking, innovative vision, and ability to implement advanced technologies place him</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">among the leading IT professionals in the Republic of Kazakhstan”.</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38277r69">69<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:TokayevLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38277r69">351<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:TokayevLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38281r70">70<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:TokayevCV --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38281r70">354<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:TokayevCV --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 234--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Azamat Sanatov. Consultant, Department for Protection of Information Resources,</text:span>
<text:span text:style-name="underline" >Administration of the President of the Republic of Kazakhstan</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 237--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Azamat Sanatov states that he worked with Mr. Taximov in an interagency group on building network
infrastructure for central government bodies during the pandemic period, when Mr. Taximov served as
Deputy Chairman of the Management Board of JSC “Astana Innovations” overseeing IT and
telecommunications development in Astana.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 239--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Sanatov highlights Mr. Taximov’s contribution to backbone connectivity and reliability,
stating:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 240--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Mr.</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> Taximov proposed a project to build a modern structured cabling network that ensures reliable</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and high-speed data transmission. He recommended deploying 100</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> Gb/s Ethernet switches, which</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">increased network fault tolerance to 99.99%’.’</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 244--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He further describes perimeter-security modernization at ministerial networks and its multi-agency
impact:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 245--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“We also worked with Mr.</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> Taximov on implementing next-generation firewalls that provided</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">comprehensive protection of the network perimeter of ministries by preventing unauthorized access</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and cyberattacks, while enabling real-time traffic monitoring and control. As a result of this project,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">we increased the level of cybersecurity of 11 government institutions, improved data transfer speed,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and created a flexible and scalable network infrastructure”.</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 249--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Finally, Sanatov credits Mr. Taximov with data-center modernization for e-government-critical
systems:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 250--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“One of Mr.</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> Taximov’s significant contributions was the development and implementation of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">digital project &#x0022;Data Center&#x0022;, which ensured high fault tolerance and uninterrupted operation of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the IT infrastructure of government bodies and key electronic-government information systems.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">He proposed equipping these data centers with advanced solutions, including backup power supply,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">climate  control,  and  physical  security,  which  significantly  reduced  the  risk  of  data  loss  and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">downtime of critical services” [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38345r86"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">86</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38345r86"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">402</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">] [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38349r87"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">87</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovCV --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38349r87"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">405</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovCV --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">].</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 255--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Recognition by Kaspersky Lab International for Contributions to Information Security (2022)</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 258--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kaspersky Lab’s Central Asia office issued Mr. Taximov a signed and sealed Certificate of Appreciation
recognizing his contribution to the development of the information security sector. From the letter,
<text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Certificate of Appreciation </text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">… for contribution to the development of the information security industry.”</text:span></text:span>
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38353r88">88<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyThanks2022Ex --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38353r88">408<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyThanks2022Ex --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 261--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The recognition reflects Mr. Taximov’s cybersecurity leadership across multiple dimensions of practical
impact:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 265--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 266--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Improving  the  iKOMEK109  digital  ecosystem,  implementing  robust  protection  and
      monitoring tools on a citywide, 24/7 digital platform.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Public private cooperation, partnering with leading suppliers and integrators to improve
      the resilience of critical municipal services.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Institutionalization of incident response practices, standards and guidelines for public and
      quasi public organizations, including measures to ensure confidentiality and data protection.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Promoting digital literacy and security by design, extensive information and awareness
      raising activities to improve the security of public information systems.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 273--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">These contributions are consistent with Mr. Taximov’s concurrent strategic work as an Independent
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
Director at the national cyber operator (JSC “State Technical Service”), on projects such as Synaq
(security testing portal), ScanKZ (national exposure monitoring) and an internal cyber media
monitoring bot. The work involved defining security requirements, prioritizing features, coordinating
delivery across multiple teams, setting acceptance criteria, and measuring impact — project
management applied to cybersecurity platforms at national scale.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 276--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">That this recognition came from Kaspersky Lab, which is an independent, internationally
operating cybersecurity company, underscores its significance as an external, industry-level
validation of Mr. Taximov’s contributions. The company’s standing in the field is evidenced
by:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 280--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 281--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >BBC News coverage, <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Kaspersky identified the state level “Flame” malware </text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">… one of the most</text:span>
      <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">complex threats ever discovered.”</text:span></text:span> (BBC News report referencing work with the UN’s ITU)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >AV TEST Awards (2024), <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Kaspersky stood out in numerous tests in 2024, receiving a total</text:span>
      <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of nine awards.”</text:span></text:span>
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >SE Labs (Q1 2024), <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Achieved 100% Protection Accuracy, 100% Legitimate Accuracy and</text:span>
      <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">100% Total Accuracy.”</text:span></text:span> (SE Labs, Endpoint Security, Small Business Protection)</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 287--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38353r88">88<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyThanks2022Ex --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38353r88">408<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyThanks2022Ex --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38269r67">67<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVComparatives --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38269r67">345<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVComparatives --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38265r66">66<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVTest2024 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38265r66">340<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyAVTest2024 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38261r65">65<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyBBC --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38261r65">336<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskyBBC --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 290--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Accordingly, a personally addressed, signed commendation from an independent, internationally
recognized cybersecurity company such as Kaspersky constitutes credible external validation of Mr.
Taximov’s significant and recognized contributions to the information security field.

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.5.2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-230002.5.2" name="x1-230002.5.2"></t4htlink>AI technologies</text:h> 

<!--l. 297--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov led complex AI and analytic projects across industry and municipal environments.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 300--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Dmitry Panchenko. Systems Integrator (Target AI video analytics and urban enforcement)</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 302--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Integrator Dmitry Panchenko, with whom Mr. Taximov worked for over seven years, describes Mr.
Taximov as an <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“architect of the digital future”</text:span></text:span>. Regarding their joint work, Mr. Panchenko
writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 303--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Among  the  recent  joint  projects,  I  would  like  to  especially  highlight  the  project  on  the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">implementation of the Target AI video analytical system within the framework of complex and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">information support of the vital activity of the city of Astana”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 307--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Panchenko details the specific scale and technical execution under Mr. Taximov’s leadership:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 308--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar led this pilot project for the last 3 years... In the framework of the implementation of the Target</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">AI pilot project, Askar successfully completed the following tasks:</text:span>
     </text:p> 
<!--l. 311--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">connected more than 600 digital video surveillance cameras, located in various districts of</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the city. To determine the location points of digital cameras, Askar used analytical modules</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of the HPSM information platform, where information about incidents comes from residents</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of the capital;</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">integrated specialized technical modules of Target AI for facial recognition, smoke detection</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and  ‘lost’  objects,  ensuring  their  uninterrupted  operation  and  compliance  with  such</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">international standards as IEC 60529 and PAL;</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">developed and implemented a strategy for optimizing the video stream processing system,</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">which provided for the use of artificial intelligence algorithms”.</text:span></text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 317--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Regarding the impact of this system on city safety and enforcement, Mr. Panchenko attests that: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“The</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">system increased the detection of violations by license plate numbers by 37% and recorded</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">3,755 cases of unauthorized waste unloading by freight transport using artificial intelligence</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">algorithms”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 320--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Concluding his assessment, Mr. Panchenko emphasizes Mr. Taximov’s strategic and analytical strengths,
stating: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar Taximov possesses unique skills in strategic thinking and innovative problem-solving,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">which enabled him to effectively coordinate the development and implementation of IT projects. He</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">demonstrates exceptional analytical and technical capabilities, allowing him to accurately set</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">priorities and develop innovative approaches to solving complex challenges”.</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38293r73">73<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PanchenkoLetter --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38293r73">363<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:PanchenkoLetter --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 324--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Dr. Chingiz Kenshimov. Computer vision PhD and co-founder and technical lead of Verigram</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 326--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Computer vision PhD and co-founder and technical lead of Verigram Dr. Chingiz Kenshimov describes
Mr. Taximov’s role in their AI startups ABY Applied Systems and Verigram. He credits Mr.
Taximov with defining product concepts, directing the research group, and building scalable
architectures:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 327--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar Taximov... successfully identified market needs, developed product concepts, and set the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">technical direction for the research team... In particular, he helped us in the development of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">products related to video analytics and assessment of urban traffic flows, which were implemented</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">jointly with Cisco and underwent tests on the roads of Almaty”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 331--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Regarding the technical infrastructure and architectural engineering, Dr. Kenshimov writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 332--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“At Verigram, he was responsible for developing and optimizing modular code that ensured system</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">scalability and high load support. He developed the architecture of software solutions based on</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">modern frameworks such as TensorFlow and PyTorch... Within the context of work on ABY</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Applied Systems, Askar developed a hybrid architecture of server interaction with cloud and local</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">computing, which allowed to significantly increase data processing speed... and implemented a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">microservice approach”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 336--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Dr. Kenshimov highlights Mr. Taximov’s specific contribution to machine learning operations (MLOps)
and model performance:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 337--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Also an impressive contribution... was the creation of an effective pipeline for data processing,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">including automatic data labeling, model training and their subsequent integration into commercial</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">solutions. His work ensured an increase in the accuracy of model predictions by 15%, which led</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">to improved product quality and customer satisfaction”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 341--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Finally, Dr. Kenshimov highlights Mr. Taximov’s expertise, noting: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar Taximov possesses</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">unique professional skills and extensive experience, which make him a valuable asset to any</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">large organization or project. I am confident that his expertise and specialized knowledge, as</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">well as his ability to think strategically and develop innovative solutions, will help achieve</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">outstanding results in the field of IT technology development”.</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38297r74">74<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38297r74">366<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38301r75">75<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovCV --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38301r75">369<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovCV --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 345--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Kakhar Kashimov. CTO, Chief Software Architect, “KazDream Technologies” LLC</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 347--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kakhar Kashimov attests to Mr. Taximov’s technical leadership in developing advanced hardware and
software innovations. He highlights Mr. Taximov’s critical role in a joint startup focused on wireless
seismic exploration, describing the project’s significance and Mr. Taximov’s architectural
contributions:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 348--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“The main essence of this project consisted in the introduction of a wireless seismic exploration</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">system...  using  wireless  terrestrial  Wi-Fi  geophones,  representing  seismic  vibration  sensors,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">instead of multi-kilometer expensive cables. In this project, Askar dealt with key technical and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">innovative  issues,  such  as  high-density  seismic  wave  analysis,  data  collection  and  analytics,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">increasing the number and density of data collection nodes in difficult terrain conditions. To</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">ensure high data transfer speed... Askar proposed using a two-level system structure... utilizing</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">LPWAN, Wi-Fi LTE... allowing the construction of large-scale wireless networks with a large</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">number of data collection nodes. This technical solution allowed our project to solve key questions</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">on ensuring the required network bandwidth and its scaling... and independent data collection</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">channels”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 352--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Kashimov further details Mr. Taximov’s work on “Life Signal,” a critical safety integration project
involving global technology ecosystems:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 353--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Our next joint IT project was the Life Signal service for Android and iOS platforms, implemented</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">with the participation of Google and Apple, aimed at emergency response and interaction of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">112 emergency services with citizens’ calls, rational distribution and use of emergency services</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">resources. This project has a large-scale level since the system assumes precise determination of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the calling subscriber’s location and reduces response time”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 357--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Finally, Kashimov provides an overarching assessment directly linking Mr. Taximov’s work to
substantial, ongoing contributions to advanced technology systems, stating: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Considering the above, I</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">can confidently state that Askar Taximov has made a substantial contribution to the field of technology</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">transfer and advanced IT systems and, to this day, continues to participate in the development</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and improvement of modern information technologies”.</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38285r71">71<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38285r71">357<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38289r72">72<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharCV --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38289r72">360<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharCV --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.5.3    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-240002.5.3" name="x1-240002.5.3"></t4htlink>City scale digital governance and portfolio management</text:h> 

<!--l. 366--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov led large IT portfolios that govern how a capital city handles requests, elections, and smart
city analytics.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 369--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Yesset Baiken. Deputy Mayor of Astana (Administration of Astana city)</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 371--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Yesset Baiken describes Mr. Taximov’s city-scale digital governance impact through iKOMEK109’s
function as the city’s unified situation center, where Mr. Taximov’s leadership strengthened (1)
executive-level escalation of urgent resident issues and (2) measurable improvements in municipal
operations, public safety, and cross-agency performance.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 373--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken frames iKOMEK109 as a governance infrastructure that combines citizen intake, integrated
monitoring, and Big Data analytics connected to city leadership decision-making.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 374--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“iKOMEK is the city’s unified full-scale Situation Center and includes: (1) the iKOMEK109</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">unified contact center for life-support issues [more than 2.2 million requests per year; an analogue</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of 3-1-1 in the United States]; (2) the iKOMEK109 monitoring Situation Center, where the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">city’s  CCTV  cameras,  fire  suppression  systems,  and  Internet-of-Things  monitoring  solutions</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">are  integrated  for  round-the-clock  safety  and  continuity-of-services  monitoring;  and  (3)  the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">iKOMEK109 Analytics Center, a forecasting and analysis unit that works with Big Data to identify</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">systemic problems and escalate issues to the city leadership in order to continuously improve the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">capital’s safety and living conditions”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 378--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken highlights a specific governance mechanism introduced under Mr. Taximov that brings the most
urgent resident problems to the Mayor’s weekly executive meeting and accelerates closure of
high-priority issues.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 379--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“A new practice was introduced whereby, on a weekly basis, the Mayor’s executive meeting is</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">briefed on the most urgent and high-profile problems raised by residents, ensuring timely and deep</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">involvement of the relevant municipal enterprises; and as a result of the ‘Decision-Making Matrix’</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">method developed by Askar, by the end of 2023 and the first half of 2024 we reduced the number</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of ‘Critical’ and ‘Highly Urgent’ issues from 112 to 27, i.e., by 76%”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 383--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken further describes how Mr. Taximov modernized resident-request management and reduced
longstanding backlogs through governance-aligned digital tooling and analytics reporting.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 384--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Based on accumulated experience, Askar Taximov proposed developing dedicated functionality in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the HP Service Manager system for processing resident requests and surfacing this information</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">in analytical reports; and in 2023 a total of 426,542 requests were closed, which is 28.4% more</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">than in 2022 (332,178 requests)”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 388--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken also links Mr. Taximov’s situational center modernization to measurable public-safety
outcomes and direct fiscal impact, enabled through digital platforms and standardized operating
instructions.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 389--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As  a  result  of  modernized  monitoring  and  data-processing  algorithms  and  new  operating</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">instructions for video surveillance, the number of registered cases related to identifying drug</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">stashers through CCTV increased by 17% compared to the previous year; in 2023 the center</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">assisted in solving 23 criminal cases and 19,384 administrative offenses (13,015 formalized by</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">protocol), and due to Askar’s efforts 52,008,750 tenge in paid administrative fines was transferred</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">to the budget through digital platforms”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 393--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Concluding, Baiken explicitly attributes the organization’s outcomes and performance indicators to Mr.
Taximov’s management and innovation. <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I note that the above projects, achievements, and high</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">performance indicators are the direct result of Askar Taximov’s effective management; and due to his</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">innovative solutions, the organization ensured technological development and digital transformation”.</text:span></text:span>
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38305r76">76<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BaikenLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38305r76">372<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BaikenLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38309r77">77<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BaikenCV --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38309r77">375<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BaikenCV --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 400--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Anuar Beisenbayev. Director of Development Department, City Monitoring and Rapid Response Center iKomek109</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 402--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Anuar Beisenbayev describes Mr. Taximov’s city-scale digital governance impact through (1)
modernization of iKomek109’s citizen request management and (2) data-driven portfolio execution for
election-readiness, where Mr. Taximov’s applied systems and algorithms improved the accuracy of
critical city records and citizen-facing services.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 404--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Beisenbayev highlights Mr. Taximov’s role in building and implementing a new CRM platform for
managing citizen appeals and automating operational processes at iKomek109.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 405--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Within his work at iKomek109, he made a significant contribution to the development and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">implementation of a new CRM information system for managing citizen requests and automating</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">processes. The use of modern technologies such as React, TypeScript, Next.js, Prisma, Tailwind</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">CSS, and PostgreSQL made it possible to create a flexible and high-performance platform that</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">improves the quality of public service”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 409--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Beisenbayev further describes a citywide election-readiness effort where Mr. Taximov applied GIS
systems and data automation to correct records and raise accuracy during the electoral
period.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 410--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“He played a key role in updating information in the state database of individuals for the city</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of Astana, as well as in forming the voter list and organizing interaction with government bodies</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">as part of preparation for elections. Thanks to this, it was possible to correct more than 50 000</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">addresses and accurately link them to the relevant polling stations, which eliminated errors in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">voter lists and increased their accuracy from 84% to 100% during the electoral period”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 414--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Beisenbayev also notes that Mr. Taximov built supporting automation and citizen-facing access channels
for this governance workflow.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 415--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar developed a data filtering algorithm using the programming languages Java, Python,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">JavaScript, and SQL, which made it possible to promptly exclude from the list citizens who do not</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">meet legal requirements (for example, minors, incapacitated persons, prisoners, deceased persons,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">etc.). In addition, online services and chatbots in Telegram were created, which significantly</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">simplified for citizens the ability to check their polling station and obtain the necessary information</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">about it”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 419--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Concluding, Beisenbayev emphasizes the high level professional skills of Mr. Taximov, writing: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I can</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">assure you that Askar is a professional and expert in his field, a specialist with excellent communication</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">skills, capable of effectively coordinating work between different departments and stakeholders.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">His commitment to professional development, attention to detail, and focus on results make</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">him a valuable employee in any team. I am confident that Askar Taksimov’s knowledge of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">information technology, high level of expertise in innovative projects, experience, and leadership</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">qualities make him one of Kazakhstan’s best specialists in the field of information technology</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development and infrastructure project management”.</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38313r78">78<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BeisenbaevLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38313r78">378<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BeisenbaevLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38317r79">79<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BeisenbayevCV --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38317r79">381<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BeisenbayevCV --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 424--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Azat Kudaibergenov. Chief Inspector, Department of Digitalization and Information Technologies of Astana</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 426--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Azat Kudaibergenov describes Mr. Taximov’s city-scale digital governance impact through applied data
systems that modernized voter list management and strengthened operational coordination in municipal
service delivery, while also influencing adoption beyond Astana.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 428--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kudaibergenov describes a city project to update Astana’s voter lists and highlights Mr. Taximov’s
original algorithmic approach and cross-database integration.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 429--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Our cooperation began with joint work on an information project to update the voter lists of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">city of Astana, the idea and development of which are described in detail in his scientific oriented</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">article ‘How to use the Geonomics information system to update and generate information about</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">city residents’. In the article about this system, Askar Taximov first proposed an innovative</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">algorithm for automatically updating residents’ data, which not only improved the accuracy of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">voter lists, but also created a basis for digital planning of urban infrastructure”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 432--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Its implementation made it possible to form lists of citizens based on a single source, excluding</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">‘door-to-door’ visits and ensuring the relevance of data in real time”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 434--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He further describes Mr. Taximov’s iKomek109 governance model and the operational technologies
implemented to coordinate city services.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 435--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In  the  article  ‘How  to  apply  information  technology  tools  in  improving  the  life  of  a  city.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">iKomek  experience’  Askar  Taximov  presented  an  innovative  model  of  an  information  center</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">based on a three-level request processing system. Askar developed thorough processing algorithms,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">information architecture, and interaction mechanisms to promptly respond to citizen requests. He</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">also implemented a video surveillance and GPS monitoring system to coordinate the work of city</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">services”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 439--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kudaibergenov says that the approach became a model for replication. <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Moreover, the iKomek109</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">experience was recognized as successful and became an example for the creation of similar centers in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">other cities of Kazakhstan”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 442--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kudaibergenov concludes underscoring his significant contributions: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Finally, it is undeniable that Askar</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Taximov’s efforts are aimed at creating a favorable environment for the development of the IT industry</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">in Kazakhstan. Thanks to his work, the city of Astana is becoming one of the leaders in the field of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">digital transformation in Kazakhstan, and his projects and initiatives serve as an example for other</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">regions of the country striving to develop the IT industry.”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38321r80">80<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KudaibergenovLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38321r80">384<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KudaibergenovLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38325r81">81<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KudaibergenovCV --></t4htlink>,
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38325r81">387<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KudaibergenovCV --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 449--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Ainur Sidelkovskaya. IT and Big Data Specialist (Government-level AI &#x0026; Big Data Programs)</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 451--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Ainur Sidelkovskaya, a government scale AI and Big Data specialist with more than 15 years of
experience implementing enterprise analytics and data platforms, frames Mr. Taximov’s
work as directly aligned with modern data governance and smart city delivery models. She
emphasizes his ability to integrate operational systems into a functioning municipal service
layer, an area that intersects with her own Big Data and digital government practice. She
writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 452--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
  <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“At  iKOMEK109,  Askar  facilitated  the  development  of  key  digital  technologies  and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">telecommunications infrastructure, demonstrating a remarkable capacity for integrating complex</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">system”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 456--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">She further links his iKOMEK109 work to practical and operational outcomes related to service delivery
and citizen facing effectiveness rather than isolated technical tasks: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As well as the management of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">constructing a call center and making sure that communication with the IT sector occurs, he converted</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the call center into a very effective mechanism for enhancing the quality of life for the local</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">inhabitants”.</text:span></text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 459--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">From a data governance perspective, Sidelkovskaya highlights Mr. Taximov’s work on Geonomics as a
proposed methodology for maintaining reliable citizen data that serves as an essential prerequisite for
analytics, decision support, and smart city program execution:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 460--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In his groundbreaking article, “How to use the geonomics information system to update and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">generate citizen data” Askar addressed the critical challenge of maintaining accurate and up to</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">date citizen data, a fundamental requirement for effective urban governance”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 464--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">She underscores that his contribution is not theoretical but positioned as a set of practical mechanisms
for integrating, verifying, and using data across fragmented municipal environments:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 465--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“He offers specific, practical solutions to overcome real world problems associated with collecting,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">integrating, and verifying data. This has enormous implications for a variety of areas — from</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">resource allocation and emergency response to long-term urban development strategies. Askar’s</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">ideas are especially relevant in the context of modern trends such as smart city initiatives and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">digital government programs. As a result, his work offers a roadmap for cities looking to harness</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the power of data to govern more effectively”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 469--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Given her own background leading government-scale Big Data programs and implementing analytics
platforms for major public and private institutions, her assessment provides an expert, field-specific
validation of the significance of Mr. Taximov’s municipal data-governance and smart-city integration
work.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 470--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“... I am convinced that Askar is among the top 10% of specialists in Kazakhstan in the field of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">IT, digital technologies, urban management and innovation projects. Askar’s contribution to the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development of digital and IT technologies in Kazakhstan is as he initiates and implements projects</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">aimed at improving the quality of life of city residents. He actively shares his experience and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">knowledge with the professional community and promotes the development of young IT specialists.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">He approaches complex urban problems using principles and concepts from modern urban science</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and IT technology. With his extensive understanding of modern complex city challenges, he is</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">able to solve their problems. Askar Taximov demonstrates standards of professionalism that are</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">second to none. To illustrate, he is very meticulous and detail oriented with all his undertakings.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Achieving unmatched results is both his passion and main priority. He causes these advancements</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">because of his strong desire to innovate and lead others to embrace multiple emerging concepts</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">which I believe makes his ideas unique and important for the industry” [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">82</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">390</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">[Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38333r83"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">83</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaCV --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38333r83"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">393</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaCV --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">].</text:span>

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.5.4    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-250002.5.4" name="x1-250002.5.4"></t4htlink>National level NextITSM platform or Information System authorship</text:h> 

<!--l. 477--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Another significant contribution in the field is the development of an original IT service management
platform known as NextITSM. The Kazakh National Copyright Office issued Certificate No. 54827 for
the NextITSM platform. This official document is dated February 18, 2025. It registers the computer
program titled NextITSM. The certificate records the creation date as December 5, 2024. It lists the
authors as Anuar Beisenbayev, Askar Taximov, and Bill Seitkazin. This registration confirms national
ownership of the software. It grants exclusive intellectual property rights to the listed authors. The
government document provides objective confirmation. It states that Mr. Beisenbayev is a co author of
an original, enterprise grade IT service management platform. NextITSMAuthorCertificate Exhibit
Here
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 479--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">NextITSM is a platform aligned with the Information Technology Infrastructure Library (ITIL). It
automates the full request and incident lifecycle for service organizations. This includes registration,
execution, monitoring, and analytics. The platform controls service level agreements (SLA) and
prioritizes tasks. It manages lifecycle statuses, problem management, and root cause analysis. It also
provides knowledge base mailings and external integrations. The platform offers analytics, key
performance indicators (KPIs), and role based access. NextITSM runs across the entire iKOMEK109
system. Call center operators, municipal service providers, and government agencies use it daily. In 2024,
the system processed over 2,326 000 citizen requests. It achieved about 82% first contact resolution. The
system made 98% on time referrals. It integrated more than 12 000 digital cameras. It also
supported new AI based predictive monitoring. Figures from early 2025 show continued
growth. These results are not general call center numbers. They show the documented effect of
the ITIL aligned workflows. These workflows, automation, and traceability are built into
NextITSM.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 483--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Taken together, the evidence in this section shows that Mr. Taximov delivered sustained, measurable
improvements in Astana’s city-scale digital governance and portfolio execution through mission-critical
civic platforms and cross-agency coordination, reflecting excellence in IT project management. This
excellence was formally recognized at the highest levels of government, including presidential
commendations for national-scale initiatives and official recognition by the Mayor of Astana for his
contributions to city digital infrastructure and successful execution of the 2022 extraordinary
presidential election.

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.6    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6" name="x1-260002.6"></t4htlink>Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s authorship of scholarly articles in the field, in professional or major
trade publications or other major media</text:h> 

<!--l. 65--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov has authored 13 scholarly and scientific articles that have been published in VAK
peer-reviewed journals and conferences related to the field. The topics of these publications include
smart-city analytics, municipal data engineering, open data and APIs, cybersecurity, and civic IT
productization.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 67--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The Higher Attestation Commission (VAK) under the Ministry of Science and Higher Education
of the Russian Federation is a national body responsible for scientific attestation. Among
its core functions, VAK establishes requirements for peer-reviewed scientific journals and
maintains an official list of journals approved for the publication of dissertation research
for the degrees of Candidate of Science and Doctor of Science (PhD). Journals included
in the VAK list are subject to editorial oversight and peer review standards [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38357r89">89<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:VAKList --></t4htlink>,
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38357r89">411<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:VAKList --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 69--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Each publication listed below is included in the VAK register, as evidenced on the journals’ official
websites and the screenshots provided as exhibits. This confirms that the articles were published in
recognized scholarly journals with established editorial oversight.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 73--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Methodology for creating an effective IT ecosystem under resource constraints”</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov, A.A. Beisenbayev), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Vestnik of Technological University</text:span></text:span>, Vol. 28, No. 4,
2025.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 76--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Vestnik of Technological University</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed scientific journal publishing research
in engineering and information technologies. The article presents a methodology for building operational
IT platforms under limited financial and time resources. It addresses technology selection,
data organization for real-world workloads, phased system deployment, and management of
technical debt to maintain long-term system stability. The paper further describes a practical,
phased approach centered on delivering an MVP with open technologies and an Agile Scrum
delivery model under tight budget and staffing constraints. It highlights an implementation
case with compressed timelines and a small team structure, emphasizing performance and
scalability objectives under limited infrastructure. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38361r90">90<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldTU --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38361r90">414<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldTU --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38365r91">91<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldTUSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38365r91">417<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldTUSite --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 80--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Information technology tools to improve urban life: iKomek experience”</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov, D.R. Satvaldina), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Components of Scientific and Technological Progress</text:span></text:span>,
No. 4(94), 2024.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 83--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Components of Scientific and Technological Progress</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed scientific journal
published quarterly. The article analyzes the organizational and technical structure of the
iKomek civic contact center, including omnichannel intake, request prioritization, responsibility
assignment, and management dashboards. It traces the full lifecycle of a citizen request
from initial contact to escalation to the city situation center and identifies architectural
elements applicable to other municipalities. The article additionally outlines a structured,
multi-level processing model in which operators receive requests, specialized teams manage
complex cases, and organizations maintain end-to-end accountability for issue resolution. It also
explains how the platform incorporates multiple communication channels and operational
control tools, including reporting dashboards for city leadership and coordination using
video and GPS monitoring where applicable. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38369r92">92<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ComponentsScientific --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38369r92">421<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ComponentsScientific --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38373r93">93<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ComponentsScientificSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38373r93">424<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ComponentsScientificSite --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 87--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Geonomics: address-registry maintenance and population heat-map analytics</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >for smart-city operations”</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov, A.A. Beisenbayev), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Engineering Bulletin of the Don</text:span></text:span>, No. 9,
2024.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 91--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Engineering Bulletin of the Don</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed electronic scientific journal published by
the North-Caucasus Research Center of Southern Federal University.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 93--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The article introduces the Geonomics system and proposes an integrated methodological and
algorithmic framework for maintaining up-to-date population and address data in large urban
environments. The proposed model combines address registries, digital cartography, and government
databases into a unified analytical platform that reduces inconsistencies in citizen registration data,
minimizes manual errors, and improves the accuracy of territorial population analysis. The paper
presents original algorithms for data standardization, polygon-based spatial analysis, automated
voter-to-address linkage, and population heat-map generation, enabling reliable association of residents
with administrative units and supporting data-driven urban planning and public service allocation. In
addition, the article proposes a methodology for automated synchronization of residency data through
structured integration with government registries, significantly improving data timeliness and
consistency. The described geospatial subsystems demonstrate practical effectiveness in planning social
infrastructure such as schools and hospitals, contributing to more efficient use of municipal
resources and improved service accessibility. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38377r94">94<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:VestnikDona --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38377r94">427<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:VestnikDona --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38381r95">95<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:VestnikDonaSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38381r95">430<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:VestnikDonaSite --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 98--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Possibilities of using open data: the concept of e-Democracy in smart-city management”</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov, A.A. Beisenbayev), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Innovations and Investments</text:span></text:span>, No. 11, 2023.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 101--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Innovations and Investments</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed journal focused on economics, management,
and innovation.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 103--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The article examines the role of open data in smart city governance and proposes a conceptual and
architectural model for transitioning from passive data publication to an integrated, API-driven open
data ecosystem. The proposed approach addresses key limitations of traditional open data
portals, including data fragmentation, low reuse, and limited civic engagement. The article
introduces an integrated open data architecture that consolidates heterogeneous datasets using
ETL-based processing, standardized formats, and controlled API access, enabling secure
and scalable data reuse while ensuring regulatory compliance. In addition, it proposes a
citizen-centered governance framework that incorporates feedback mechanisms and dataset interaction,
demonstrating how open data can support transparency, civic participation, and participatory
decision making in smart city management. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38385r96">96<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:InnovationInvestment --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38385r96">435<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:InnovationInvestment --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38389r97">97<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:InnovationInvestmentSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38389r97">438<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:InnovationInvestmentSite --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 108--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Big data as a smart-city management tool”</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov, A.A. Beisenbayev), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Science and Business: Development ways</text:span></text:span>, No. 1(151),
2024 (section: Mathematical modeling and numerical methods).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 111--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Science and Business: Development ways</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed journal used for publishing
dissertation research. The article demonstrates how large-scale urban data can be applied as an
operational management instrument. It connects data analytics to key performance indicators,
planning processes, and resource allocation, describing end-to-end data pipelines and governance
mechanisms across transport, social support, and municipal services. The paper further
proposes concrete analytic use cases such as forecasting transport-network load using large-scale
transaction and monitoring signals and using integrated data to identify high-risk anomalies in
the urban environment. It also describes how big-data pipelines can support cross-agency
operations, including public safety and social-service decision making, by turning heterogeneous
city signals into actionable planning inputs. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38393r98">98<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ScienceBusiness --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38393r98">443<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ScienceBusiness --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38397r99">99<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ScienceBusinessSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38397r99">446<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ScienceBusinessSite --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 115--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Information technologies for updating and forming address information”</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov, A.A. Beisenbayev), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Herald of Computer and Information Technologies</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">(VKIT)</text:span></text:span>, 2024, pp. 52–62 (DOI: 10.14489/vkit.2024.03.pp.052-062).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 118--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Herald of Computer and Information Technologies</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed monthly journal
focused on computer and information technologies. The article presents a data engineering system and
algorithmic methodology for election period voter list formation that addresses incomplete and error
prone registry data. The proposed solution integrates multiple government datasets into a unified
pipeline with automated filtering, validation, and rule based exclusions aligned with electoral legislation.
The article describes an end to end process for data extraction, normalization, eligibility
filtering, and geographic assignment of voters to polling stations, significantly reducing manual
intervention and human error. As a result, voter list accuracy increased from 84 percent to
100 percent during the election period. The article also outlines supporting public services,
including a dedicated support center and digital verification tools, which enhanced transparency,
citizen trust, and operational efficiency. [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38401r100">100<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldOfCIT --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38401r100">450<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldOfCIT --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38405r101">101<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldOfCITSite --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38405r101">453<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HeraldOfCITSite --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 122--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Efficiency improving strategy of international technology transfer in cybersecurity”</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Automation. Modern Technologies</text:span></text:span>, No. 2(80), 2026, pp. 77-84
…(DOI:10.36652/vkit.004.05)
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 125--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Automation. Modern Technologies</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, long-running peer-reviewed scientific and technical
journal focused on automation and modern information technologies. The article analyzes the challenges
of cross-border cybersecurity technology transfer under conditions of sanctions and limited
access to foreign technological solutions and proposes a structured model to mitigate these
constraints. It proposes cooperative models involving research centers, industry, and open-source
tools, and provides structured recommendations for strengthening national cybersecurity
capabilities. The article further develops a hybrid transfer model that combines external
technology scouting, localized adaptation hubs, and a multi-stakeholder consortium approach
to accelerate adoption while reducing dependency risks. In addition, the article outlines
practical implementation mechanisms, including controlled parallel engineering where legally
permissible and systematic participation in open-source ecosystems. These mechanisms are
presented as effective tools for strengthening national cybersecurity capacity and improving
resilience under restrictive international conditions. [Exhibit <text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">??</text:span>, page <text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">??</text:span>] [Exhibit <text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">??</text:span>, page <text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">??</text:span>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 129--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Scientific paper: “Technology to integrate artificial intelligence into smart city control centers</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >for faster decision-making”</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>(A.B. Taximov), published in: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Information Systems and Technologies</text:span></text:span>, 2026, No. 1(153) …
</text:p> 
<!--l. 133--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Information Systems and Technologies</text:span></text:span> is a VAK-listed, peer-reviewed scientific journal of Orel State
University focused on information systems and information technologies. The article addresses
information overload in smart city control centers and presents an author developed methodology for
integrating artificial intelligence into decision support workflows. The proposed approach supports
operators in high intensity monitoring environments by structuring and prioritizing heterogeneous data
streams while preserving human decision making. The article describes a modular architecture that
integrates automated data collection, machine learning analytics, computer vision, predictive
models, and a scenario based knowledge base within a unified operator interface, enabling the
transformation of raw event streams into prioritized and explainable recommendations. An
illustrative incident handling scenario demonstrates the full decision support cycle from event
detection to operator confirmation. The human in the loop design reduces cognitive load and
response time by filtering non critical information while keeping final decisions under operator
authority.
</text:p> 
<!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.7    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-270002.7" name="x1-270002.7"></t4htlink>Evidence of Mr. Taximov’s performance of a leading or critical role for organizations with a
distinguished reputation</text:h> 


                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.7.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-280002.7.1" name="x1-280002.7.1"></t4htlink>Municipal State Enterprise “iKOMEK109” City Monitoring and Rapid Response
Center</text:h> 

<!--l. 9--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">iKOMEK109 is the capital city’s unified citizen-service and operational situation hub, combining 24/7
intake, real-time situational awareness (CCTV/IoT), and Big-Data analytics for systemic-issue detection
and escalations to city leadership. The Deputy Mayor’s letter describes the organization’s scope
explicitly:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 10--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“iKOMEK represents the city’s unified Situation Center comprised of: (1) the iKOMEK109</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">contact center [more than 2.2 million citizen requests per year], (2) the monitoring Situation</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Center with integrated camera networks, fire-prevention systems and Internet-of-Things solutions,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and (3) the Analytics Center that works with Big Data to identify systemic issues and escalate</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">them to the city’s leadership”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 14--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Independent materials corroborate iKOMEK109’s official mandate and scale: the national government
portal confirms iKOMEK109 as the consolidated 24/7 single contact point for municipal
enterprises, lists the official omnichannel intake (109 short number, Akimat website, Telegram bot,
iKOMEK109 and Smart Astana mobile apps, email), and reports a 2,500+ service catalog with 85%
first-call resolution. Major press coverage reports million-scale request throughput, and the
verified Instagram profile evidences sustained public-facing operations (230K followers, 5,937
posts). Accordingly, given its citywide mandate, million-scale annual request throughput,
omnichannel public operations, and formal integration into the Akimat’s 24/7 situation and
decision-support infrastructure, iKOMEK109 is widely regarded as a major, distinguished
municipal organization in Astana [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38213r53">53<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekGov --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38213r53">285<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekGov --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38229r57">57<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekPress --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38229r57">299<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekPress --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38217r54">54<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekInstagramShot --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38217r54">288<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 16--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">As a Head-IT Project Manager of iKOMEK109, Mr. Taximov held a critical leadership role with control
over core operational, technology, and governance functions. Deputy Mayor of Astana city confirms Mr.
Taximov’s leadership position and emphasizes that his role is not merely technical, but executive and
transformation-oriented:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 18--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar  Taximov  has  been  the  Head  of  the  City  Monitoring  and  Rapid  Response  Center</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">‘iKOMEK109’  since  May  27,  2022.  During  his  tenure,  he  has  proven  himself  to  be  a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">highly professional and effective leader who makes significant efforts toward the digitalization,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">technological transformation, and innovative development of the company”.</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 22--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken describes the scope of what iKOMEK109 is responsible for and the kinds of city operations it
coordinates and controls:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 23--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As part of the first stage of the technological transformation of the Akimat of the city of Astana,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the ‘iKOMEK109’ Center was created, the main areas of activity of which are the reception of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">residents’ requests, the coordination of the work of municipal and emergency services in resolving</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">incidents and accidents, the control of timely closure of incidents and the identification and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">processing of incidents of offenses, and the building of a policy of preventive measures as well as</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">operational control over the situation in the city in the ‘here and now’ mode through the city video</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">surveillance system”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 27--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He explicitly attributes enterprise-wide optimization and service-quality improvements to Mr. Taximov’s
leadership after his appointment:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 28--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“From the moment of Askar Taximov’s appointment to the position of head of the iKOMEK</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">center, a course was taken toward significant optimization of processes and improvement of work</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">in key areas such as the implementation of innovative solutions and increasing the efficiency of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">processing problematic issues, which made it possible to significantly improve the quality of services</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">provided and interaction with the structural divisions of the Akimat”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 32--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken further documents Mr. Taximov’s city-level project governance leadership through the formal
transformation and operation of a project management department:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 33--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“At the beginning of 2023, by the decision of the Akimat of the city, the Project Office of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Akimat of the city of Astana was transformed on the basis of iKOMEK109 into the Project</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Management Department. The main goal of the Department is to ensure effective interaction and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">coordination of all participants in project activities in the implementation of city development</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">programs by applying project management methods and tools. Under the leadership and effective</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">coordination of Askar Taximov, Scrum meetings were held with the structural divisions of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Akimat to manage projects in the information system using a project approach, through which key</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and strategic projects as well as activities to achieve KPI were determined. In addition, project</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">charters were developed, projects were decomposed into specific tasks with deadlines, work with</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">stakeholders was carried out, and project templates with central government bodies were developed”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 37--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken confirms the scale of stakeholders involved in the project-governance system coordinated through
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
iKOMEK109:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 38--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Currently, 23 departments of the Akimat, 5 district Akimats, 2 territorial departments (the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Police Department and the Department for Emergency Situations), and 75 quasi-public sector</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">companies are involved in the implementation of project management.”</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 42--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken describes a governance method introduced by Mr. Taximov for closing urgent municipal
problems and quantifies its results:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 43--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As a result of the ‘Decision-Making Matrix’ method developed by Askar, for the results of 2023</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and the first half of 2024 we were able to reduce the number of current problems under the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">‘Especially Important’ and ‘Very Urgent’ criteria from 112 to 27, that is, by 76%”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 47--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken also provides quantified evidence of operational throughput improvements and closure of citizen
requests:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 48--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“At the end of 2023, 426 542 requests were closed, which is 28.4% more than in 2022”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 52--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken documents citywide infrastructure outcomes tied to iKOMEK109’s systemic problem resolution
work:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 53--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As a result of this decision, from July 1, 2022, 31 systemic problems were closed, more than</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">80 children’s playgrounds were modernized, and 43 sports grounds were reconstructed. Lighting</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">with a length of 378 km was installed in problem areas, which significantly improved safety and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">comfort for residents and reduced the crime rate by 27.3%”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 57--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He reports expansion of the city’s surveillance infrastructure and its integration into city digital
processing systems:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 58--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“The number of video surveillance cameras was increased from 9 752 to 10 581 (by 8.5%), and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">they were integrated into the city’s digital data processing system”.</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 62--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken describes safety-related operational improvements and law-enforcement support, including
quantified results:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 63--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As a result of process changes, the number of registered reports on the capture of drug ‘stash’</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">dealers using video surveillance cameras increased by 17% compared to the previous year. By the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">end of 2023, assistance was provided in solving 23 criminal offenses and 19 384 administrative</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">offenses, of which 13 015 were documented by protocol. Due to Askar’s efforts, 52 008 750 tenge</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of paid fines were transferred to the budget using digital platforms based on issued administrative</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">protocols”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 67--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken highlights that Mr. Taximov created internal technology capacity by establishing an R&#x0026;D
department and applying modern Data Science and Big Data tools, producing measurable improvements
in citizen data accuracy:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 68--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Another important unique and significant contribution of Askar Taximov to the sustainable</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development of the company iKOMEK109 was his creation in 2022 of a new structural subdivision,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the ‘Department of IT and Development (Research and Development Department),’ which on an</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">ongoing basis updates the voter list in the territory of the city of Astana by identifying incorrect</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">or outdated registration addresses of citizens and assigning them an address registration code. In</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">its work, the Department uses advanced tools in the field of Data Science and Big Data, including</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">programs and technologies such as Python, R, Apache Hadoop, Apache Spark, TensorFlow, as</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">well as SQL and NoSQL databases”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 72--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He describes that Mr. Taximov built internal product-development capacity and led the modernization
of the iKOMEK 2.0 digital ecosystem, writing:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 73--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Also, on the initiative of Askar Taksimov, the iKOMEK109 center began to specialize in the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development of modern digital technologies and IT development. He formed a full-fledged team of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">qualified web developers and programmers, whose task was to modernize the current iKOMEK 2.0</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">ecosystem. To achieve this goal, Askar developed and approved a roadmap with clear deadlines and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">specific executors, which includes the following blocks:</text:span>
     </text:p> 
<!--l. 76--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">creation of a new version of the CRM system for more efficient reception of applications</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">from residents;</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">ensuring integration with external services;</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development of a tool for analyzing and managing requests and forming a rating of managers;</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">optimization of the current system’s database;</text:span>
     </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

     <text:list-item>
     <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">creation  of  convenient  online  channels  with  an  intuitive  interface  and  unified  user</text:span>
     <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">registration”.</text:span></text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 83--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Currently, the CRM system is fully released and processing daily requests 24/7, which is on average
around 7000 requests (2 500 000 annually).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 85--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Moreover, besides his executive and technology-transformation responsibilities described
above, Mr. Taximov delivered high-impact and critical improvements within the company:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 88--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Increased inclusion by raising the number of employees with disabilities from 6 to 10.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Expanded  the  youth  workforce  pipeline  by  scaling  the  youth  practice  program  to  60+
      participants.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Reduced  the  backlog  of  long-unresolved  “Waiting”  requests  by  initiating  closure  with
      complete responses to residents. He also added HP Service Manager functionality so these
      cases could be processed correctly and reflected in analytics reports (including “Waiting”
      closures marked as “does not comply”).
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Institutionalized  weekly  escalation  of  the  most  urgent  resident  issues  to  the  Akim’s
      leadership meeting. Using the “Decision-Making Matrix”  method, iKOMEK109 reduced
      “Especially Important” and “Very Urgent” problems from 112 to 27 across 2023 and the first
      half of 2024, a 76% reduction.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Strengthened  public  infrastructure  improvement  by  actively  promoting  the  “Budget  of
      People’s Participation”  program. From July 1, 2022, this work helped close 31 systemic
      problems, modernize 80+ children’s playgrounds, and reconstruct 43 sports grounds.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Formed cross-agency working groups to inspect problem zones, set priorities, and embed
      them into multi-year budgeting for systematic rollout. This approach delivered 378 km of
      new street lighting in problem areas and reduced crime by 27.3%.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Identified and coordinated fixes for systemic water supply and wastewater issues across the
      city. The letter reports 4 systemic problems identified and 3 successfully resolved, including
      high-complaint zones generating 3 000+ resident requests.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Accelerated closure of hazardous open manholes by organizing accountability workflows
      to identify responsible asset holders. Over the last two years, 13 927 open manholes were
      eliminated, and the average closure time was reduced by two times.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Improved situational-center performance by updating monitoring and analytics algorithms,
      optimizing registration and processing workflows, and issuing new operating instructions for
      video-based incident response. As a result, camera-based detections related to drug “stash”
      activity increased by 17% compared to the previous year, and in 2023 the center supported
      23 criminal cases and 19 384 administrative offenses, with 52 008 750 KZT in paid fines
      transferred to the budget through digital platforms.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Increased adoption of digital intake channels through a strategy focused on messengers and
      social media, including continuous monitoring of city public channels, feedback collection,
      awareness posts, and campaigns. This work increased requests via the Telegram chatbot
      and the iKOMEK109 mobile app by 22% in 2023 compared to the previous year.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Improved staff performance and motivation by defending the budget and linking incentives
      to KPI performance. Since June 1, 2022, salaries increased by 51% for production staff and
      by 31% for administrative and managerial staff, and rank-and-file employees became eligible
      for bonuses of up to 4 monthly salaries.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Secured housing-support access for employees by signing a cooperation memorandum with
      Otbasy  Bank.  This  enabled  voluntary  payroll-to-deposit  savings  toward  housing  down
      payments and raised the employee loyalty index to 42.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Launched  a  healthcare  innovation  collaboration  that  created  a  direct  resident-to-clinic
      channel and improved appointment workflows. In the pilot phase, 150+ calls per week were
      processed in 4 medical organizations.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 103--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Baiken directly links iKOMEK109’s “high performance indicators” and transformation outcomes to Mr.
Taximov’s management effectiveness and innovation: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I note that the above projects, achievements, and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">high performance indicators of the company are the direct result of the effective management of Askar</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Taximov, and thanks to his innovative solutions the company was able to ensure technological</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development and digital transformation.”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38413r103">103<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekDeputyAkimLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38413r103">460<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekDeputyAkimLetter --></t4htlink>]

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.7.2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-290002.7.2" name="x1-290002.7.2"></t4htlink>Joint Stock Company “State Technical Service” National Cybersecurity Operator</text:h> 

<!--l. 111--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">STS is a distinguished, national-scale cybersecurity operator. State Technical Service (STS)
is a national cybersecurity organization with a long-standing public mandate to protect
Kazakhstan’s information space and the security of “electronic government” systems and
critical information and communication infrastructure. STS publicly describes its mission as
“ensuring Kazakhstan’s information security since 2008” and “creating a secure digital space
by utilizing advanced technologies and cybersecurity expertise,” and it lists national-scale
functions such as unified e-government gateways, state security testing of informatization
objects, incident monitoring and coordination, operation of national coordination centers, and
information-security certification support [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38237r59">59<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38237r59">310<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSSiteShot --></t4htlink>]. STS also maintains an active public
communications footprint, including a public Instagram presence (1,232 posts shown in the record),
supporting the organization’s prominence and sustained public-facing operations [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38241r60">60<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSInstagramShot --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38241r60">316<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 115--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">As an Independent Director and Board Member, Mr. Taximov held a critical leadership role overseeing
cybersecurity directions and strategic development.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 116--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In the position of independent director and member of the Board of Directors of the Joint Stock</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Company ‘State Technical Service’ (hereinafter – JSC ‘STS’), Askar Boranbayevich Taximov has</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">been working since January 18, 2022, on the basis of the order of the Chairman of the National</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Security Committee of the Republic of Kazakhstan dated January 14, 2022. Within the framework</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of his work, Askar Taximov implements innovative projects and coordinates the company’s areas</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">on issues of information and cybersecurity, and also heads the Strategic Development Committee</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of the Board of Directors.”</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 120--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek describes an automation tool designed for continuous collection of information-security
signals from official internet sources and Telegram media channels, implemented for routine use by STS
units:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 121--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Taking into account his experience and knowledge in the field of innovative and technological</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">solutions, Askar Taximov was involved in the implementation of a Telegram bot for monitoring</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">mass media, intended to automate the processes of searching for news regarding information</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">security topics by specific tags from official Internet resources and Telegram channels of mass</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">media. This Telegram bot was implemented for the subdivisions of JSC ‘STS’ and is used in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">everyday activities.”</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 125--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek explains that Mr. Taximov participated in the creation of a portal that digitized and
streamlined a compliance-critical testing service for e-government and critical infrastructure systems,
reducing manual paperwork:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 126--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In  addition,  Askar  Taximov  participated  in  the  development  of  the  Synaq  Internet  portal,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">implemented to automate the process of providing the service of testing informatization objects</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">of  ‘electronic  government’  and  information  systems  classified  as  critical  information  and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">communication  infrastructure  objects  for  compliance  with  information  security  requirements.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Development  of  Synaq  made  it  possible  to  automate  the  testing  process,  significantly  reduce</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">document flow, and it is used in the activities of JSC ‘STS’ ”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 130--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek highlights Mr. Taximov’s key role in the development of ScanKZ components, a
national-scale system for collecting information about exposed devices and vulnerabilities to support
analysis and prevention:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 131--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As part of cross-sector coordination on issues of monitoring information security provision,</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">protection, and the safe functioning of the Kazakhstan segment of the Internet, in 2023 JSC ‘STS’</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">carried out work to develop the ScanKZ search system for collecting information on the security</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">level of devices connected to the Internet at the scale of the Kazakhstan Internet segment. Askar</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Taximov played a key role in the development of components of this system. As a result of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development of ScanKZ, an improvement in the current activities of KZ-CERT for preventing</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">computer security threats was achieved due to the automatic identification of vulnerable objects in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the network”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 135--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In addition to the three flagship projects described above, the STS letter documents several
further contributions that strengthen the “critical role” showing (1) national-level governance
trust, (2) strategic oversight authority, and (3) practical operational impact on cybersecurity
monitoring, compliance testing workflows, and KZ-CERT’s threat-prevention capability:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 138--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Helped implement a media-monitoring automation that runs tag-based searches every 4
      hours (and can be configured, including real-time monitoring if needed).
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Enabled automated discovery of cybersecurity-relevant mentions in official online sources
      by integrating Google Programmable Search Engine queries on a recurring schedule.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented an internal workflow that alerts STS staff with a direct link whenever a tagged
      keyword is detected in news/posts, improving speed of awareness and triage.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Supported building a complete internal monitoring stack for this workflow, including a
      closed Telegram bot for managing tags/keywords and a closed Telegram chat where staff
      review the detected posts in an internal channel.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Ensured the monitoring solution includes a database for storing collected news/posts and
      tag data, creating an auditable and searchable internal history.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Introduced   operational   controls   for   this   monitoring   tool   by   implementing   user
      management (add/remove users) and action logging, strengthening internal governance and
      accountability.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Helped design Synaq as a full system with core infrastructure components, including a
      unified  data  repository  and  an  administration  module  for  managing  users  and  logging
      actions.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Supported an end-to-end digitized workflow in Synaq where applicants can form, approve,
      sign,  and  submit  requests  and  applications  for  testing,  reducing  reliance  on  manual
      coordination.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Enabled automatic cost calculation for electronic price quotations in Synaq, reducing manual
      pricing work and standardizing quotation logic.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Enabled applicants to download electronic protocols generated from testing results through
      Synaq, making compliance documentation accessible in a structured digital format.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Contributed to ScanKZ capabilities that automatically collect and display technical security
      signals such as open ports and services, TLS/SSL certificates, WHOIS data, operating
      systems,  subdomains/DNS  records,  and  IP  addresses,  improving  the  completeness  of
      exposure assessment.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Strengthened  KZ-CERT’s  operational  follow-through  by  supporting  a  system  that  can
      inform  and  warn  device  owners  when  vulnerabilities  are  discovered,  promoting  faster
      remediation after detection.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 152--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Zhunisbek concludes that Mr. Taximov’s technical expertise and innovative approach directly supported
goal attainment and increased STS effectiveness in key operational directions:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 153--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In  the  course  of  performing  the  above  tasks,  Askar  Taximov  demonstrated  a  high  level  of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">analytical thinking and professionalism, and his technical knowledge and innovative approach made</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">it possible to achieve the set goals and, overall, to increase the efficiency of the activities of JSC</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">‘STS’ in certain areas of activity”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 155--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38421r105">105<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSRoleLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38421r105">466<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSRoleLetter --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.7.3    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-300002.7.3" name="x1-300002.7.3"></t4htlink>Limited Liability Partnership “Elorda Qurylys Kompaniyasy” Municipal Developer</text:h> 

<!--l. 161--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">EQK is a distinguished, city scale municipal developer with a high visibility public mission. Elorda
Qurylys Company (EQK) is a municipal developer created to resolve problem shared equity housing,
finance and finish stalled construction sites, and deliver apartments to equity holders. Public facing
materials document continuous operations since 2018 and a sustained public mission focused on
completing problematic projects and delivering housing under the city’s development framework
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38245r61">61<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38245r61">319<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKSiteShot --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 164--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">EQK’s public record corroborates the organization’s mandate and execution at scale. Public materials
report completion of 141 residential buildings and re-housing of 15 500+ families, establishing EQK as
the city’s principal mechanism for resolving problem projects. The official website presents
EQK’s mission and a portfolio of delivered residential complexes (for example, completed
projects showing apartment counts, status, and delivery dates), confirming the breadth and
continuity of EQK’s operations. EQK also maintains a sustained public communications footprint
through its verified Instagram profile, evidencing ongoing stakeholder engagement and high
visibility public activity. The screenshot in the record shows 468 posts (as of 2025)[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38249r62">62<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKInstagramShot --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38249r62">324<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 167--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov was appointed into a senior executive role at EQK, with delegated authority over both
financial management and IT modernization, rather than a routine technical position:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 168--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“During his period of activity, from March to June 2022, Askar held the position of First Deputy</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">General Director for financial and IT issues. In this relatively short time, he proved himself to be a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">highly qualified manager with the ability to find non-standard, innovative solutions and implement</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">modern approaches in the company’s work”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 172--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Tauekelov documents that Mr. Taximov secured large-scale financing that directly enabled completion of
problematic facilities and delivered housing outcomes for thousands of families:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 173--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar managed to obtain financing totaling 51 billion tenge from the National Fund of the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Republic of Kazakhstan and the local budget. These funds made it possible to successfully complete</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">work  on  10  problematic  facilities,  including  27  residential  buildings.  As  a  result,  more  than</text:span>
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">3000 families received the keys to their long-awaited apartments, obtained new housing, and the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">opportunity to start a new chapter of their lives”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 177--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Tauekelov further explains that Mr. Taximov implemented a digital financial governance system that
materially reduced costs and accelerated project delivery timelines:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 178--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“He  developed  and  implemented  a  digital  financial  model  in  the  company,  which  ensured</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">transparency  and  targeted  allocation  of  funds  from  the  National  Fund  of  the  Republic  of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Kazakhstan, and from the republican and local budgets. After the implementation of the new</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">model, which made it possible to control the budget in real time, forecast costs, and optimize</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">logistics, the company reduced these costs by 30%, which led to savings of 156.9 million tenge</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">annually. In addition, accurate planning and detailed data analysis made it possible to reduce the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">average commissioning time of facilities by 11% - from 24 months to 21 months. As a result of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the implementation of the digital financial model, the company not only saved 156.9 million tenge,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">but also accelerated work processes, which led to profit growth of 7–9%”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 182--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Tauekelov also describes how Mr. Taximov expanded completion capacity by attracting investors and
enabling delivery through partnership with a major developer:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 183--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Thanks to his negotiation and communication skills, Askar attracted investors totaling 30 billion</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">tenge,  which  allowed  the  company  to  complete  another  8  problematic  facilities,  including  12</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">multi-apartment residential complexes. He managed to attract the largest developer in Kazakhstan</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">— BI Group”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 187--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Tauekelov further documents that Mr. Taximov implemented real-time construction transparency and
remote monitoring that reduced complaints and improved site security and safety outcomes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 188--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In addition, he ensured transparency of the process for equity holders, allowing them to watch</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the construction progress in real time through a video surveillance system using Computer Vision</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">technology. The introduction of online viewing reduced the number of complaints from equity</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">holders by 35%. According to operational reports of law enforcement agencies, the number of thefts</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">at construction sites decreased by 46%. The level of industrial injuries decreased on average by</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">2.3 times”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 192--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Finally, Tauekelov describes Mr. Taximov’s introduction of BIM as a modern digital capability that
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
reduced design and approval risks:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 193--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“One of Askar’s important achievements was the implementation of the digital BIM product</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">(Building Information Modeling — information modeling technology), which allowed our company</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">to effectively manage construction projects at every stage of their life cycle. Thanks to these</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">solutions,  errors  and  risks  during  the  passage  of  project  expertise  decreased  by  3.5  times  in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">authorized bodies”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 197--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In addition to the described above, the EQK letter documents further contributions that demonstrate
sustained operational impact, modernization of governance, and measurable improvements in
citizen-facing trust and construction safety:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 200--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Analyzed EQK’s business processes and split them into functional blocks, which the letter
      links to fixing weak cross-department coordination and improving cost control.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Built  a  structured  planning  system  with  normative,  indicative,  and  descriptive  plans,
      including plan–fact analysis and financial forecasting.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Added vertical and horizontal analysis and introduced financial health indicators (liquidity,
      stability,  profitability  ratios)  to  create  a  complete  picture  of  the  company’s  financial
      condition.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Digitalized the entire financial governance model in 1C:ERP, automating data collection
      and management for end-to-end control. Implemented multi-level planning horizons inside
      the system (strategic, medium-term, short-term, tactical, and operational) so management
      could plan and manage funds across timeframes. Configured a Target Indicators Monitor
      and defined key metrics for each planning level to standardize performance tracking.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Integrated and upgraded the Budgeting module with the financial system so leadership
      could view the company’s financial position in dashboards and charts.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Defined operational control metrics inside the model, including funds raised, construction
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      volume, procurement plans, number of facilities, suppliers, fixed assets, credit operations,
      indirect-cost reduction, and profitability, enabling detailed analytics by activity block.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >The letter notes the pre-existing problem he addressed: weak coordination and inefficient
      cost management caused annual losses of about 10% of the construction budget, stated as
      523 million KZT.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Developed a 10-step BIM implementation algorithm, from customer request for a BIM model
      through life-cycle updates and archiving of the digital model.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented BIM in a Common Data Environment (CDE) with role-based access, giving
      architects, engineers, and builders real-time access to current project data and improving
      coordination. The letter provides a specific BIM case: the 2022 “Turan–Syganak” residential
      complex was modeled using Model Studio Soft (four modules, including CADlib Model
      &#x0026;  Archive),  producing  a  detailed  3D  model  that  covered  buildings  and  surrounding
      infrastructure elements.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 211--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Tauekelov concludes by emphasizing the exceptional and irreplaceable nature of Mr. Taximov’s
contribution to EQK’s transformation and results:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 212--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In conclusion, I want to emphasize that Askar’s contribution to the development of the company</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">was invaluable” [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38425r106"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">106</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKRoleLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38425r106"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">469</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:EQKRoleLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">].</text:span>

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--start of subsubsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-4" text:outline-level="4" ><text:span text:style-name="subsubsection" >2.7.4    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-310002.7.4" name="x1-310002.7.4"></t4htlink>Joint Stock Company “Astana Innovations” Smart City Operator</text:h> 

<!--l. 221--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">JSC “Astana Innovations” is a distinguished, city-scale Smart City operator with sustained public
mandate. Astana Innovations functions as the city’s Smart City operator, responsible for core municipal
digital infrastructure, including the Big Data platform, the evolution from open data to open APIs, and
the telecom-duct infrastructure that underpins broadband connectivity. This is not a narrow
internal IT unit, but a city-facing operator tasked with maintaining and expanding shared
platforms used across municipal domains. The Board Chairman’s recommendation letter further
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
documents the organization’s mandate, scope, and the concrete programs delivered under Mr.
Taximov’s leadership [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38429r107">107<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINRoleLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38429r107">472<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINRoleLetter --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38253r63">63<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38253r63">327<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINSiteShot --></t4htlink>]. Astana Innovations’
official public materials corroborate its institutional role and continuity of operations. The
organization’s official website publicly presents its mission and scope across Smart Astana initiatives,
Big Data, Open Data/Open APIs, and telecom-duct management, and it also publishes
standard corporate-governance information and operational disclosures consistent with a
city-scale operator. These public disclosures align with the institutional remit described in the
recommendation letter and support the organization’s distinguished reputation as the city’s platform
steward rather than a project-based contractor [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38253r63">63<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINSiteShot --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38253r63">327<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINSiteShot --></t4htlink>]. Astana Innovations
also maintains an official public communications presence through its Instagram account
“astana.innovations” identifying the organization and linking to its official domain. As of 2025, the
account reflects 836 posts, supporting the organization’s visibility as the city operator [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38257r64">64<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINInstagramShot --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38257r64">333<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:AINInstagramShot --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 226--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">JSC “Astana Innovations” is a city-scale innovation integrator created to advance Kazakhstan’s
innovation economy and implement “Smart Astana” initiatives. The organization states:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 227--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Our company JSC “Astana Innovation” was established in 2011 for the purpose of developing</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">competitiveness and creating the most favorable conditions for the implementation of innovations</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">in the economy of the Republic of Kazakhstan. The responsibility of the company makes it possible</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">to integrate all available government instruments for supporting innovations for the successful</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">implementation of projects at the city level. This enables the capital to make a breakthrough in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the field of new technologies”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 231--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kaldybayev, CEO of the Company, describes Mr. Taximov’s critical role in scaling AIN’s Big Data
platform into a multi-source analytical system with measurable outputs:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 232--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“JSC “Astana Innovations” is the operator of a Big Data platform, which represents a set of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">tools for data analysis and visualization, including the “Tulpar” cartographic system, which was</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">developed in 2018. He personally initiated further improvement of a platform capable of processing</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and analyzing large volumes collected from various city sources, which is about 76 databases. This</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">product allowed our company to effectively identify trends, forecast needs, and develop targeted</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">development strategies based on factual data”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 236--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“With  Askar’s  unique  knowledge  and  efforts,  as  a  result  12  analytical  data  models  were</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">implemented  and  an  additional  block  of  text-and-graphic  visualization  of  information  was</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">created. All these measures made it possible to resolve pressing issues in the field of passenger</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">transportation and increase transportation efficiency on average by 17%”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 240--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“As a result, TOP-40 addresses were identified in which 76 thousand people are registered. From</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">government data sources, he identified a list of large families in the city in the amount of 14</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">601 families. Then he determined relationships with information about children to form a family</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">passport, the number of which is 92 957 children”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 244--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“All the above-listed results and achieved successes were obtained thanks to the professional</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">efforts, experience, and high expertise of Askar Taximov, as well as his persistence and innovative</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">solutions”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 248--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kaldybayev also explains that Mr. Taximov expanded the citizen-facing Smart Astana platform by
proposing and implementing new services aligned with resident needs:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 249--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Within the framework of the “Smart Astana” concept, our company developed and launched a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">portal and a mobile application of the same name. These innovative solutions serve as a single</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">interface for providing city services and public services, based on the principle “the whole city in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">your smartphone”. After carefully studying the current services and the needs of city residents,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Askar Taximov proposed creating new services that would expand the functionality of the portal</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and the mobile application”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 253--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“For  example,  under  Askar’s  supervision  a  service  for  checking  the  queue  number  as  well</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">as  accepting  documents  for  enrollment  in  kindergartens  and  schools  of  the  city  of  Astana</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">was implemented. In city hospitals, QR-code-based technologies were introduced, through which</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">residents can scan a QR code in the “Smart Astana” mobile application and leave feedback about</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the doctor’s work”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 257--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Thanks to this development, a systemic problem of falsification of medical certificates No. 086</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and No. 083, as well as sick leave certificates and sanitary books, was solved”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 261--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Beyond digital services, Kaldybayev documents Mr. Taximov’s operational modernization with
quantified improvements in telecom infrastructure management:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 262--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“JSC ‘Astana Innovations’ is designated as the city’s managing company for the operation of cable</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">duct infrastructure, which plays a key role in providing stable and high-speed internet, telephone</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">communications, and other telecommunication services. Askar organized a phased reduction of</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the time for reviewing applications and issuing technical conditions from 30 calendar days to 14</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">days. Thanks to Askar’s efforts and determination, the number of agreements increased from 20</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">to 73, and total income reached from 38 million tenge to 152 million tenge in 2021, thus in a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">short period the city’s cable duct activity moved from “loss-making” to “profitable”.</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 266--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In addition to the flagship outcomes described above, the AIN letter documents further Askar Taximov’s
contributions showing breadth of impact across Smart City service delivery, data governance, and
election operational readiness:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 269--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Built a Big Data decision-support stack that unified 104 data layers (from 76 databases)
      and displayed them on the city’s digital map.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Created an “Identifying the Self-Employed”  Big Data model and delivered an export of
      identified  self-employed  residents  to  the  Astana  City  Employment  Center  for  follow-up
      action.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Modernized the city transport decision-support system by updating the “Transport Model”
      and integrating it into the digital map with real-time stop-level load visibility, enabling
      route planning and improving passenger transportation efficiency by an average of 17%.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Developed a machine-learning approach to resolve inconsistent address spellings (up to 6
      variants for the same street) and used it to detect “rubber apartments”, identifying TOP-40
      addresses where 76 000 people were registered and transferring this information to migration
      authorities for verification.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Built a Big Data “Profile of Large families”  identifying 14 601 large families and linking
      child data to form family passports covering 92 957 children, including geocoordinates and
      map-based analytics for social-support planning. As a result of this profiling tool, social
      protection agencies gained map-based capabilities to see where large families live, track
      children counts, form a mother’s passport, and plan support programs based on identified
      needs.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented open-data automation by converting city data outputs into Open API services
      (not  only  file  downloads),  enabling  users  to  retrieve  up-to-date  data  automatically  via
      scripts, while still supporting downloads in .xls, .csv, and .json.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Delivered  a  public  open-data  portal  that  provides  20  datasets  across  9  categories  (e.g.
      education, healthcare, transport, housing and communal services, city services, internet,
      ecology, news/events), expanding structured access to city data.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Implemented an analytics workflow for election-related online services using Elasticsearch
      + Kibana, and built a daily Python (Pandas) log-processing script that loads service logs
      into PostgreSQL for SQL-based reporting by Individual Identification Number, district, and
      city.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Improved voter registry accuracy in Astana from 84.4% (Jan 1, 2020) to 100% (Dec 1, 2020),
      raising the capital from last place to a leading position by registry relevance.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Updated  address  records  for  50  000+  citizens  by  assigning  address  registration  codes
      and  synchronizing  corrected  data  into  the  national  “Individuals”  database  through
      migration-service corrections.
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Enabled  automated  precinct  assignment  by  adding  geolocations  for  8  000+  building
      addresses on the precinct digital map, and he also reduced precinct over-capacity issues by
      cutting the number of precincts exceeding the constitutional norms from 101 to 10.</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 282--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Kaldybayev concludes by directly tying these results to Mr. Taximov’s professionalism and high value to
the organization:
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 283--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“All the above-mentioned results and achievements of our company are directly related to the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">high professionalism and diligent contribution of Askar Taximov. His merits in our company are</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">invaluable and deserve a high assessment”.</text:span>

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsubsection--><!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.8    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-320002.8" name="x1-320002.8"></t4htlink>Comparable evidence of public display of work</text:h> 

<!--l. 60--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Under 8 C.F.R. § 204.5(h)(4), when a criterion in § 204.5(h)(3), such as artistic exhibitions or
showcases, does not directly apply to the occupation, USCIS may consider comparable evidence.
IT-related work and applied research are not typically presented in artistic exhibitions. Instead,
professionals in this field publicly display their work through technical conference presentations,
scholarly papers, and industry forums, where project architectures, methodologies, and implementation
case studies are presented and archived in citable proceedings or repositories. Therefore, the materials
below demonstrate evidence of comparable public display.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 64--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the conference “Digitalization and technological revolutions: current challenges</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >and opportunities”, 12 July 2025.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes the paper “How to detect multi-level cyber threats in real time with AI and
behavioral pattern analysis”. The paper presents an author-developed artificial intelligence–based
detection methodology for real-time identification of complex, multi-level cyber threats using behavioral
pattern analysis instead of static signature matching. It proposes a system architecture and detection
logic that analyze behavioral deviations across multiple layers to identify coordinated and
previously unknown attack patterns. The paper also reports an experimental evaluation
comparing the proposed AI-based approach with traditional detection methods, demonstrating its
effectiveness in identifying sophisticated threats in dynamic environments. The conference
was organized by the International Centre for Innovative Research “Omega Science,” and
the proceedings were published as a citable volume available through academic libraries
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38433r108">108<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:program1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38433r108">475<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:program1 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38437r109">109<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38437r109">478<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate1 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38441r110">110<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38441r110">481<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection1 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38445r111">111<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma1 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38445r111">484<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma1 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 70--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the International Scientific practical conference “World science: Problems and</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Innovations”, 30 May 2025.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes the paper “Algorithm for Developing post-quantum cryptography to protect critical
infrastructure against quantum attacks”. The paper proposes a lattice-based cryptographic approach
designed to improve resilience against future quantum-computing threats. It outlines the
mathematical model, algorithmic structure, and performance characteristics in comparison with
existing cryptographic schemes. The conference was organized by the International Centre for
Scientific Cooperation “Science and Education” and the proceedings were publicly released
with bibliographic records [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38461r115">115<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate3 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38461r115">496<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate3 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38465r116">116<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection3 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38465r116">499<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection3 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38469r117">117<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma3 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38469r117">502<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma3 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 76--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the conference “Modern technologies in technical and natural sciences”,</text:span> <text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >5 June 2025.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>At the conference, A. Taximov presented the work “Optimization of cloud system performance
using adaptive machine learning algorithms.”. The paper addresses the practical problem
of maintaining stable cloud performance under rapidly changing workloads and proposes
applying adaptive ML methods to automate key optimization decisions, including workload
forecasting, resource auto scaling, database query optimization, and anomaly detection, thereby
reducing manual tuning and performance degradation. The conference was organized and
proceedings were published as a citable volume by the International Institute for Advanced Studies
named after Lomonosov [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38449r112">112<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate2 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38449r112">487<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate2 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38453r113">113<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection2 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38453r113">490<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection2 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38457r114">114<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma2 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38457r114">493<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma2 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 82--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the National Scientific practical conference “Modern methods and innovations</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >in science”, 12 May 2025.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes the paper “Mechanism of accelerated transfer of technologies from scientific
laboratories to industry of Kazakhstan”. The conference proceedings identify the included materials
as selected scientific works recommended for publication by the editorial and publishing
council of the Humanitarian National Research Institute “Natsrazvitie.” The paper presents
an author-developed mechanism for accelerating technology transfer in Kazakhstan and
proposes a model approach built around the creation and integration of the Technology
Transfer Ecosystem Platform. This proposed platform model is designed to reduce barriers to
commercialization by structurally linking science, industry, and the state within a single
ecosystem. The paper outlines the stages of technology transfer, defines the functions of key
participants, and specifies the infrastructure and regulatory conditions required to implement the
model, with the expected result of faster and more coordinated commercialization of scientific
developments in Kazakhstan. The conference was organized by the Humanitarian National
Research Institute “Natsrazvitie” [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38481r120">120<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate5 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38481r120">511<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate5 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38485r121">121<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection5 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38485r121">514<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection5 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38489r122">122<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma5 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38489r122">517<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:diploma5 --></t4htlink>].
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 88--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the International scientific practical conference “Scientific Forum: Innovative</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Science”, No. 6 (85), 28 June 2025.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes the paper “Methodology of data transfer protocol standardization for cross-platform
integration of IoT devices”. The paper proposes a standardized protocol framework for interoperable
communication among heterogeneous IoT devices. It describes protocol architecture, integration
mechanisms, and system-level efficiency improvements. The conference proceedings list the paper in the
official table of contents, and the electronic version is archived in national scientific repositories and
academic databases, confirming its formal publication and public availability. The conference was
organized by the International Centre for Innovative Research and Publishing “MCNO” and published as
part of a citable international scientific proceedings volume (ISSN 2542-1255) [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38473r118">118<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate4 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38473r118">505<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:certificate4 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38477r119">119<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection4 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38477r119">508<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:collection4 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 94--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the Forum “Profit Contact Day 2025: New technologies in contact centers”,</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >13 June 2025.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes a report and presentation titled “Digital transformation of a city platform: experience
of creating iKOMEK 2.0”. The official program and event materials document the public presentation of
his work, including coverage of his on-stage presentation. The presentation publicly showcased the
architecture and implementation approach for upgrading a municipal contact-center platform into
iKOMEK 2.0, including digital workflow redesign, omnichannel service logic, and modernization of the
city platform’s operational model for citizen requests. The forum was held in Almaty at the
InterContinental hotel in offline and online format, with 200+ offline participants and 1000+ online
viewers, and focused on innovative technologies for contact centers, including AI and automation
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38113r28">28<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitContactDay2025 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38113r28">184<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitContactDay2025 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 100--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the conference “Profit Smart City Day 2024”, 11 October 2024.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes presentation with a title “Smart City: The role of the iKOMEK109 situation center in
ensuring city safety and identifying housing and utility problems”. The presentation materials, together
with an official invitation letter and photographic evidence, document the public display of
the work. The presentation demonstrated the architecture and operational model of the
iKOMEK109 situation center, including AI-assisted monitoring, integration of large-scale video
infrastructure, and automated coordination of municipal services. The event was organized by
Profit Events and focused on urban digital transformation in Kazakhstan [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38501r125">125<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitSmartCityDay2024 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38501r125">524<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitSmartCityDay2024 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 105--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the conference “Profit Education Day 2023”, 20 October 2023 dedicated to the</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/><text:span text:style-name="underline" >digitalization of education in Kazakhstan.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>Mr. Taximov delivered a presentation titled “iKOMEK109: education, IT, and urban development,” in
which he presented the applied use of urban digital platforms in the education sector. The presentation
demonstrated how the iKOMEK109 situation center architecture is used to monitor, analyze, and
respond to education-related incidents, including citizen requests concerning schools, kindergartens, and
educational infrastructure. The report showcased real operational data, omni-channel citizen interaction,
analytics dashboards, and interdepartmental coordination mechanisms, illustrating the practical
integration of city IT systems into education governance. The public display of the work is
documented through the official conference program, speaker listings, presentation materials, and
photographic evidence of the presentation. The event was organized by Profit Events as part of the
annual Profit Education Day forum and brought together representatives of government
bodies, universities, IT companies, and education-sector decision-makers, focusing on digital
transformation, EdTech solutions, cloud platforms, and information security in education [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38493r123">123<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitEducationDay2023 --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38493r123">520<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitEducationDay2023 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 111--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the conference “Profit Smart City Day 2023,” 15 September 2023.</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>The work includes a public presentation titled “iKOMEK109 today”. The presentation materials,
together with the official conference program, speaker listings, and video recordings, document the
public display of Mr. Taximov’s work. The presentation demonstrated the architecture, operational
model, and real-world deployment of the iKOMEK109 city situation center, including centralized intake
of citizen requests, integration with municipal and emergency services, large-scale video surveillance
infrastructure, and data-driven coordination of city services. The presentation highlighted practical
results of digital city governance, including improved incident detection, service response coordination,
and analytics-supported decision-making at the municipal level. The event was focused on digitalization
of cities, smart-city infrastructure, video analytics, urban safety, and automated public-service
management, with participation from government regulators, city administrations, and industry experts
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38497r124">124<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SmartSityDay2023 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38497r124">522<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SmartSityDay2023 --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 116--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Participation in the Digital Festival “Google DevFest Taraz 2023”, 16–17 November 2023.</text:span>
<text:line-break 
/>The work includes the presentation and technical case study “City center for monitoring and operational
response iKOMEK109 and project QalaQyzmet”. The case study describes the design and
implementation of a unified digital platform integrating municipal utility services into a single window
online “One Stop Shop”. The presentation demonstrated how the iKOMEK109 platform integrates
multiple municipal services such as housing and utilities, incident reporting, service requests, and
notifications within one coordinated digital interface. The proposed “one-stop shop” model
enables residents to submit requests, track resolution status, and receive updates across
multiple city services through a single entry point, eliminating fragmentation and reducing
response time. The case study covered system architecture, inter-service integration, secure data
exchange, and automated user-notification mechanisms, illustrating how disparate municipal
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
systems are orchestrated into a coherent operational workflow. The event was Organized
by the Governance of Zhambyl Region in partnership with Google Developers Group and
Zhambyl Hub. The goal was to foster regional digitalization and IT talent [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38505r126">126<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:GoogleDevFest --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38505r126">534<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:GoogleDevFest --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 121--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Across these events, Mr. Taximov’s own developed digital platforms, system architectures, and applied
implementation methodologies were publicly presented at scientific and industry conferences and
documented in official programs, proceedings, and event materials. Because traditional artistic
exhibitions do not apply to IT project management, these public conference presentations constitute
comparable evidence of public display under 8 C.F.R. § 204.5(h)(4).
</text:p> 
<!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >2.9    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-330002.9" name="x1-330002.9"></t4htlink>Evidence that  Mr. Taximov has commanded a high salary relative to others in the
field</text:h> 

<!--l. 5--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The following section presents independent, third-party salary benchmarks for Astana, Republic of
Kazakhstan, for the occupation of IT Project Manager. These sources establish baseline market
compensation levels in the same geographic labor market and are used for comparison against
Mr. Taximov’s documented earnings.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 10--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 10--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" >HR Praktika (Official SalaryCertificate)</text:span>  HR  Praktika  issued  a  signed  salary  certificate
      defining typical job duties and qualification requirements for an IT Project Manager in
      Astana.  The  certificate  applies  an  averaging  methodology  across  multiple  professional
      compensation  studies  (including  People  Consulting,  EY,  Habr,  and  hh.ru)  and  reflects
      prevailing base salary levels in the market.
      </text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >
           </text:p> 
<!--l. 15--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Monthly Salary: 500,000 KZT
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Annualized Total: 6,000,000 KZT [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38509r127">127<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HRPRITPM1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38509r127">537<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HRPRITPM1 --></t4htlink>]</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" >HeadHunter.kz (Official Letter)</text:span> A signed letter from HeadHunter Kazakhstan reports the 2024
      mean monthly salary for IT Project Manager positions in Astana, calculated from vacancies
      published on its national recruitment platform.
      </text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >
           </text:p> 
<!--l. 28--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Monthly Salary: 442,000 KZT
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Annualized Total: 5,304,000 KZT [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38517r129">129<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HH1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38517r129">547<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HH1 --></t4htlink>] [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38521r130">130<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HH2 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38521r130">550<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:HH2 --></t4htlink>]</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

      </text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" >RecCom Recruiting (Market Overview)</text:span> RecCom Recruiting provided a signed and sealed
      2024 market overview for Astana. The overview defines role scope and summarizes
      compensation data derived from recruitment and placement activity for IT Project
      Managers.
      </text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >
           </text:p> 
<!--l. 41--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Monthly Salary: 558,000 KZT
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Annualized Total: 6,696,000 KZT [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38525r131">131<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:RecCom1 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38525r131">553<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:RecCom1 --></t4htlink>]</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

      </text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" ><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Bureau of National Statistics (Official Government Letter)</text:span> The Department of the Bureau
      of National Statistics for Astana issued official response No. 2025 03546738 (dated
      13 October 2025). The data is derived from the nationwide <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Report on the Structure and</text:span>
      <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Distribution of Wages”</text:span></text:span> (Index 2–T) and is classified under the National Classifier of Occupation
      for ICT and project-management roles.
      </text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >
           </text:p> 
<!--l. 54--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Monthly Salary: 758,791 KZT
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
           </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

           <text:list-item>
           <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Annualized Total: 9,105,492 KZT [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38529r132">132<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BNSAstanaICTPM2024Letter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38529r132">557<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:BNSAstanaICTPM2024Letter --></t4htlink>]</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

      </text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 63--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">A formal <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Salary Statement</text:span></text:span> issued by the Municipal State Enterprise iKOMEK109 documents
Mr. Taximov’s compensation for his position titled as a <text:span text:style-name="underline" >Head-IT Project Manager</text:span> for 2024
[Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38533r133">133<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekSalary --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38533r133">561<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekSalary --></t4htlink>]:
</text:p> 
<text:section text:style-name="begin-end-env" text:name="begin-end-env-3" ><text:p text:style-name="begin-env-p" ></text:p><!--begin center-->
<text:p text:style-name="center" >
Total Gross Earnings for 2024: 36,280,907.9 KZT
</text:p><text:p text:style-name="end-env-p" ></text:p></text:section><!--end center-->
<!--l. 67--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="textit" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">The USD equivalent below is provided for reference only and is calculated using the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">National Bank of Kazakhstan average exchange rate for 2024 (468.99</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> KZT/USD)</text:span></text:span>: </text:p> 
