<table:table-cell table:style-name="hline-cell" ><text:p text:style-name="hline-p-hr" /></table:table-cell> 
<table:table-cell table:style-name="hline-cell" ><text:p text:style-name="hline-p-hr" /></table:table-cell> 
<table:table-cell table:style-name="hline-cell" ><text:p text:style-name="hline-p-hr" /></table:table-cell> 
</table:table-row> 
<table:table-row  
 table:style-name="TBL-2-6-"><table:table-cell  
 table:style-name="TBL-2-6-1"><text:p  
text:style-name="sty-11L" >                                         </text:p></table:table-cell>
</table:table-row></table:table>
<text:p text:style-name="end-env-p" ></text:p></text:section><!--end center-->
<!--l. 89--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">According to independent statistics and national wage data, Mr. Taximov’s earnings are up to
<text:span text:style-name="underline" >from 4.0 to 6.8 times higher</text:span> than the average salary in the field.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 92--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"></text:p> 
<text:p text:style-name="newpage"></text:p>
<!--l. 92--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
                                                                                              
                                                                                              

</text:p> 
<!--end of subsection--><!--end of section--><!--start of section--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-2" text:outline-level="2" ><text:span text:style-name="section" >3    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-340003" name="x1-340003"></t4htlink>Final merits determination</text:h> 

<!--l. 5--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In accordance with the Kazarian opinion, the subsecond step of the two-part approach is a
final merits determination that considers all of the evidence in the context of whether the
beneficiary meets the required level of high achievement and sustained national reputation in the
field.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 7--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The aggregated evidence establishes that Mr. Taximov not only meets the regulatory criteria, but also
that he has been recognized nationally as an authority in IT Project Management and Digital
Governance.

</text:p> 
<!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >3.1    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-350003.1" name="x1-350003.1"></t4htlink>Mr. Taximov has risen to the very top of the field of IT Project Management</text:h> 

<!--l. 13--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov is an expert of extraordinary ability who has risen to the very top of his field.
His standing is confirmed by independent experts, national recognition, and mass media
coverage.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 15--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Leading experts confirm Mr. Taximov’s extraordinary technical skills and impact.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 19--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Dr. Chingiz Kenshimov (Computer Vision PhD).</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>Dr. Kenshimov explains Mr. Taximov’s work on product architecture and leadership of research teams.
Dr. Kenshimov writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 21--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar is a true professional in information technology and innovation. His technical skills,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">strategic thinking, and ability to build scalable architectures make him one of the best experts in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the field of digitalization. He consistently proposes practical, modern solutions and then drives</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">them through implementation with high standards. His contributions have long-term impact and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">strengthen the broader digital ecosystem.” [Section</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">2.5</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">36</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">] [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38297r74"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">74</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38297r74"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">366</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 25--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Kakhar Kashimov (Chief Software Architect).</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>Mr. Kashimov (MSc, Imperial College London) highlights co-founding work with Mr. Taximov on
wireless geophone sensor networks and emphasizes his ability to translate research concepts into
large-scale, real-world systems. Mr. Kashimov writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 27--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“I confidently recommend Askar Taximov as one of the best and most competent specialists in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Kazakhstan in the field of information technology and digitalization. He consistently demonstrates</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">top-tier  expertise  and  delivers  high-impact  technology  solutions  at  scale.  He  combines  strong</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">engineering judgment with innovation, and he turns complex ideas into working systems. He</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">is a strategic technical leader whom teams rely on when outcomes must be delivered under real</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">constraints.” [Section</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">2.5</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">36</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">] [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38285r71"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">71</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38285r71"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">357</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 31--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >Azamat Sanatov (Presidential Administration).</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>Mr. Sanatov describes Mr. Taximov’s advanced capabilities in cybersubsecurity and IT infrastructure,
emphasizing that his role is both technical and methodological. Mr. Sanatov writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 33--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar is one of the best high-qualified specialists in Kazakhstan in information subsecurity,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">cybersubsecurity, and IT infrastructure. His expertise and practical leadership are recognized at</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">the highest levels and reflect standing at the very top of the field. He approaches subsecurity</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">as  a  complete  system:  policy,  process,  technology,  and  accountability.  His  work  strengthens</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">institutional resilience and helps organizations reduce exposure to cyber threats.”  [Section</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">2.5</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">36</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">] [Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38345r86"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">86</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38345r86"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">402</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovLetter --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 37--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><text:span text:style-name="underline" >A. Zhunisbek (Chairman of the Board, State Technical Service JSC).</text:span> <text:line-break 
/>Chairman Zhunisbek links Mr. Taximov to national information subsecurity projects and
confirms his strategic authority within STS governance structures. Chairman Zhunisbek
writes:
</text:p> 
<!--l. 39--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
 <text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar Taximov demonstrated a high level of analytical thinking and professionalism and played a</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">key role in the development and implementation of national-level information subsecurity systems.</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">His contribution confirms his position among top experts in the field. He is trusted with projects</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">that require both strategic oversight and technical depth. His approach improves effectiveness</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and supports the subsecure functioning of critical digital infrastructure.” [Section</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">2.5</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">36</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">[Exhibit</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38273r68"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">68</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSContribution --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">, page</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> </text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-38273r68"><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">348</text:span><!--tex4ht:ref: ex:STSContribution --></t4htlink><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">]</text:span>
</text:p> 
<!--l. 43--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">His status at the top of the field is solidified by the highest state honors and major authorship. Mr.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
Taximov was awarded the state medal “Eren enbegi ushin” (<text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">For Distinguished Labour</text:span></text:span>) by the President
of the Republic of Kazakhstan, a distinction reserved for the highest achievers in the nation
([Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">2.1<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">8<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>]).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 45--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Furthermore, he authored the NextITSM platform, a system of major significance that processed over
2.3 million citizen requests in 2024, acting as the digital backbone of the capital’s monitoring center
[Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">2.5<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">36<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 47--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov serves as a recognized authority for national strategic initiatives. His leadership role was
highlighted by <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">Forbes Kazakhstan</text:span></text:span>, which mentioned him in the context of municipal digital
transformation [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38229r57">57<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekPress --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38229r57">299<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:IKomekPress --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 49--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Consequently, Mr. Taximov is consistently invited as an expert speaker for major forums, including the
subsecurex Plenary Session, the Ministry of Defense digitalization panel, and the Digital Almaty forum
that were noted by top experts in [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">2.5<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">36<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>]. Independent experts confirm his
repeated invitations to high-profile international and national stages such as GITEX Global
and Profit Smart City Day ([Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38501r125">125<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitSmartCityDay2024 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38501r125">524<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitSmartCityDay2024 --></t4htlink>]). Ainur Sidelkovskaya notes that his
appearances at <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“prestigious venues as GITEX Global, Profit Smart City Day</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">…</text:span><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200"> always arouse keen</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">interest among the audience”</text:span></text:span>, reflecting sustained peer recognition of his authority [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82">82<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82">390<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 51--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">She further emphasizes that he <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“actively shares his experience and knowledge with the professional</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">community”</text:span></text:span>, which is why organizations repeatedly seek his expert participation [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82">82<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82">390<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink>].
Kakhar Kashimov likewise confirms that Mr. Taximov advances the field through <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“popularizing his</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">innovative ideas and developments”</text:span></text:span> and by <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“speaking at various conferences on issues of digitalization</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">and integration of IT-solutions”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38285r71">71<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38285r71">357<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KaharLetter --></t4htlink>]. These repeated invitations show that Mr.
Taximov is engaged not as a ceremonial participant, but for practical expertise in Smart City delivery,
Big Data governance, and cybersubsecurity-focused digital transformation ([Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">2.5<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-210002.5">36<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Contributions --></t4htlink>]).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 53--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The below shown documents prove that Mr. Taximov is continuously invited to various events as an
expert in the Information Technologies field:
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 55--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Digital Almaty 2024 (forum invitation). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38549r137">137<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:DigitalAlmaty2024 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38549r137">571<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:DigitalAlmaty2024 --></t4htlink>]
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Securex  2024  (invitation  and  business  program).  [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38581r145">145<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:Securex2024 --></t4htlink>,  page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38581r145">587<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:Securex2024 --></t4htlink>]  [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38585r146">146<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SecurexProgram --></t4htlink>,
      page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38585r146">589<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SecurexProgram --></t4htlink>]
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >KazHackStan 2024 (cybersecurity conference invitation). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38565r141">141<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KazHackStan --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38565r141">579<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KazHackStan --></t4htlink>]
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >GITEX 2024 in Dubai (OpenText customer delegation). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38557r139">139<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:GITEXDubai --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38557r139">575<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:GITEXDubai --></t4htlink>]
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >OpenText Europe 2024 in Prague (customer conference invitation). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38573r143">143<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OpenTextEurope --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38573r143">583<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:OpenTextEurope --></t4htlink>]
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >MOST Hub defense digitalization panel (expert invitation). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38569r142">142<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:MostHub --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38569r142">581<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:MostHub --></t4htlink>]
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Profit Infrastructure Day 2025 (conference invitation). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38577r144">144<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitInfrustructureDay --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38577r144">585<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitInfrustructureDay --></t4htlink>]
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Kaspersky Security Day 2023 (conference materials). [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38561r140">140<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskySecurityDay2023 --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38561r140">577<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KasperskySecurityDay2023 --></t4htlink>]</text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 


<!--end of subsection--><!--start of subsection--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-3" text:outline-level="3" ><text:span text:style-name="subsection" >3.2    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-360003.2" name="x1-360003.2"></t4htlink>Mr. Taximov has sustained national and international acclaim in his field of expertise</text:h> 

<!--l. 69--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov has not only achieved national acclaim but has sustained this recognition over a
continuous period, evidenced by a consistent trajectory of awards, media appearances, and expert
roles.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 71--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">His recognition by the Head of State and municipal leaders has been sustained over multiple years. Mr.
Taximov received an Honorary Diploma from the Mayor of Astana in 2022 and 2024. The President of
the Republic of Kazakhstan sent him personal Letters of Appreciation in 2022 and 2024. The President
awarded him the state medal “Eren enbegi ushin” (<text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">For Distinguished Labour</text:span></text:span>) in October 2025. These
continuous high-level awards demonstrate that he has sustained his national recognition ([Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">2.1<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-30002.1">8<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Awards --></t4htlink>]).
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 73--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">He is a recurring subject of interest for major media outlets. The media consistently seeks Mr.
Taximov’s expertise to explain complex digital trends to the public. His media presence includes various
interviews, such as a distinguished alumnus feature for L.N. Gumilyov ENU, a technical discussion on
“Smart City” technologies for HubTalks, and a live broadcast interview on iKOMEK operations for the
TV program <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">By Trends</text:span></text:span>.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 75--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov is continuously invited as an expert to guide the next generation of specialists.
Demonstrating his sustained authority, he is frequently invited to evaluate professional competitions. He
served as a speaker at Google DevFest [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38505r126">126<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:GoogleDevFest --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38505r126">534<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:GoogleDevFest --></t4htlink>] and ProfIT Day [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38577r144">144<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitInfrustructureDay --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38577r144">585<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:ProfitInfrustructureDay --></t4htlink>], and has served on an ongoing basis as an honorary jury member for the ITeachMe
Foundation’s OrleTECH finals, evaluating projects in NoCode, AI, and UX/UI design. [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4">2.4<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Judging --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-130002.4">25<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Judging --></t4htlink>]
</text:p> 
<!--l. 78--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov’s sustained acclaim is further evidenced by scholarly authorship that documents and
disseminates his original, field-tested methods for smart-city delivery and data governance [Section <t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6">2.6<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Articles --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-260002.6">51<!--tex4ht:ref: subsec:Articles --></t4htlink>]. Independent experts confirm that these were practical innovations formalized as
professional or peer-reviewed works. Dr. Kenshimov states: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“Askar Taximov published five scientific</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">articles presenting unique approaches and algorithms to improve urban infrastructure and</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">automate administrative processes”</text:span></text:span>. He adds: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In one of his papers, he developed algorithms</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">for interacting with government databases to automatically update individual citizen data,</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">significantly improving the accuracy and timeliness of these records”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38297r74">74<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38297r74">366<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:KenshimovLetter --></t4htlink>]. Mr.
Sanatov emphasizes his applied value: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“He made substantial contributions by developing</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">practical methods and instructions on urgent IT-industry problems, which were reflected in</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">his scientific and practical articles”</text:span></text:span> [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38345r86">86<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovLetter --></t4htlink>, page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38345r86">402<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SanatovLetter --></t4htlink>]. Ainur Sidelkovskaya confirms
the governance importance of this work: <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">“In his groundbreaking article, “How to use the</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">geonomics information system to update and generate citizen data”, Askar addressed the critical</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">challenge of maintaining accurate and up-to-date citizen data, a fundamental requirement for</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">effective urban governance”</text:span></text:span>. These publications show that Mr. Taximov’s solutions are not only
implemented in practice, but are formalized and disseminated as recognized methods, which is
characteristic of a top-tier expert whose work influences how others in the field operate [Exhibit <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82">82<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink>,
page <t4htlink 
href="#x1-38329r82">390<!--tex4ht:ref: ex:SidelkovskayaLetter --></t4htlink>].
</text:p> 
<!--l. 82--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The above presented evidences clearly show that Mr. Taximov has been nationally recognized as
outstanding in his field. His work has both substantial merit and national importance, directly
strengthening the country’s cybersubsecurity posture and municipal efficiency. As such, Mr.
Taximov meets the requirements for the EB-1A classification as a person of extraordinary
ability.

                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--end of subsection--><!--end of section--><!--start of section--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-2" text:outline-level="2" ><text:span text:style-name="section" >4    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-370004" name="x1-370004"></t4htlink>Mr. Taximov’s proposed employment has both substantial merit and national importance for the
United States</text:h> 

<!--l. 65--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The United States labor market demands skilled IT Project Managers. The U.S. Bureau of
Labor Statistics lists the <text:span text:style-name="underline" >2024 median pay at $100,750</text:span>. It also predicts employment growth of
<text:span text:style-name="underline" >6% from 2024 to 2034</text:span>. This rate exceeds the average for all jobs (BLS, 2024). Executing complex digital
programs requires <text:span text:style-name="underline" >local hiring</text:span> across complementary roles such as developers, delivery leads,
SRE/DevOps specialists, data engineers, ITSM administrators and cybersecurity analysts, supporting
ongoing U.S. based operations rather than one off deployments (BLS, 2024). At the same time, the
market for project management tools is expanding quickly, projected to reach <text:span text:style-name="underline" >$20.47,billion by 2030</text:span> at
an annual growth rate of <text:span text:style-name="underline" >15.7%</text:span>, with <text:span text:style-name="underline" >North America</text:span> holding 41.97% of the 2022 market (Grand
View Research, 2023). Organizations lose an estimated <text:span text:style-name="underline" >$2 trillion</text:span> annually due to failed or
underperforming projects, roughly $1 million every 20 seconds (PMI, 2024). Large studies of IT
portfolios document “black swan” overruns with severe operational and fiscal consequences across
both private and public sectors (Flyvbjerg &#x0026; Budzier, 2022 and Flyvbjerg et al., 2025). By
<text:span text:style-name="underline" >2030</text:span>, AI is expected to automate up to <text:span text:style-name="underline" >80%</text:span> of routine project management tasks, with
humans focusing on higher value strategic leadership (HBR, 2023). These trends confirm that
disciplined, AI aware IT project leadership has substantial merit for the U.S. economy. Aging
infrastructure, climate shocks, and staff shortages burden U.S. municipalities (SmartBrief, 2025 and
Zacua Ventures, 2024). Independent analyses show that Smart City tools raise efficiency by
<text:span text:style-name="underline" >20 to 3%</text:span>. The U.S. Smart Cities market alone is projected to reach about <text:span text:style-name="underline" >$260.9,billion by 2028</text:span>,
evidencing strong domestic demand for interoperable and secure platforms (MarketsandMarkets,
2024). Small and mid sized cities, in particular, need affordable and secure systems that
improve service delivery despite limited budgets and staff (Lincoln Institute of Land Policy,
2024).
</text:p> 
<!--l. 71--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov’s experience was formed in a <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">mature digital government ecosystem</text:span></text:span>. International
assessments such as the UN e-Government Survey and regional development bank analyses consistently
rank Kazakhstan among higher performing e-Government environments in Asia (UN e-Government
Survey and Asian Development Bank synthesis). Strong private sector adoption, including multi service
“super app” platforms (for example, international coverage of Kaspi.kz), complements this environment.
Within that context, Mr. Taximov has led the design and implementation of digital urban
monitoring systems, citizen service and CRM platforms, predictive analytics pipelines and
cybersecurity architectures, deployed at scale in production environments. This dual public and
private background prepares him, as an IT Project Manager, to navigate civic constraints,
regulatory requirements and market driven pressures that are comparable to those facing
U.S. jurisdictions.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 75--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The methods documented in his record include requirements baselining, KPI and SLA regimes, iterative
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
release trains, data quality pipelines, AI and analytics instrumentation and security by design. They
map directly onto U.S. initiatives to
</text:p> 
<!--l. 78--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">
      </text:p> 
<!--l. 80--><text:list text:style-name="Itemize" > 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Update  and  check  <text:span text:style-name="underline" >3 1 1 service systems</text:span>.  Handle  incidents  quickly.  Track  every  case.
      (McKinsey, 2018 and Flyvbjerg &#x0026; Budzier, 2022)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Expand reliable, low-cost <text:span text:style-name="underline" >open data programs</text:span>. They support transparency and new ideas.
      (Lincoln Institute of Land Policy, 2024)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Protect <text:span text:style-name="underline" >critical infrastructure</text:span>. Old assets face stress from weather and high demand. We
      must monitor them constantly to prevent cyber attacks. (SmartBrief, 2025)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 

      <text:list-item>
      <text:p text:style-name="Inside-itemize" >Use <text:span text:style-name="underline" >affordable digital tools</text:span> in small and medium cities. Towns should use standard software.
      Custom systems carry too much risk. (Lincoln Institute of Land Policy, 2024)
      </text:p> 
</text:list-item> 
</text:list > 

<!--l. 90--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Taken together, the above shows a strong national demand for IT project leaders, large digitalization
needs in municipal systems and critical infrastructure, and substantial economic losses from poor
execution. Within this landscape, Mr. Taximov’s demonstrated record of designing, implementing and
operating large scale municipal platforms through rigorous IT Project Management methodologies,
improving service delivery, cost control and cybersecurity, positions him to deliver quantifiable value to
U.S. jurisdictions. By leading cross functional teams, managing complex technical requirements and
ensuring on time and on budget delivery, particularly in small and mid sized municipalities,
his proposed work will help close critical modernization gaps, strengthen public services
and create skilled employment in underserved regions, thereby advancing U.S. national
interests.
</text:p> 
<!--end of section--><!--start of section--><text:h text:style-name="Heading-2" text:outline-level="2" ><text:span text:style-name="section" >5    </text:span><text:span text:style-name="texttt" ></text:span><t4htlink 
href="#x1-380005" name="x1-380005"></t4htlink>Conclusion</text:h> 

<!--l. 4--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov is a professional IT project manager recognized nationally and internationally, which
is confirmed by his awards, memberships, published materials, judging activities original
contributions, scholarly articles, leadership roles and high remuneration. He intends to continue
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
his work as IT project management in the United States. His permanent residency will be
beneficial for the digital transformation and information technology sectors in the United
States.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 7--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">Mr. Taximov fully satisfies all requirements of <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">INA Section 203(b)(1)(A)</text:span></text:span> and <text:span text:style-name="Emphasis" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecti-1200">8 CFR Section 204.5(h)</text:span></text:span>.
Please kindly approve Mr. Taximov’s petition for permanent residence under the category of an alien of
extraordinary ability.
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
</text:p> 
<!--l. 21--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body"><t4htlink 
 href="#likesection.3" name="likesection.3"></t4htlink><t4htlink 
 href="#x1-38001x5" name="x1-38001x5"></t4htlink></text:p> 
<text:section text:style-name="begin-end-env" text:name="begin-end-env-5" ><text:p text:style-name="begin-env-p" ></text:p><!--begin center-->
<text:p text:style-name="center" >
 <text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1728">Statement from Mr. Taximov detailing plans on how he</text:span>
<text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1728">intends to continue work in the United States</text:span></text:span>
</text:p><text:p text:style-name="end-env-p" ></text:p></text:section><!--end center-->
<!--l. 24--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">My name is Askar Taximov. I am the beneficiary of this I-140 Immigrant Petition for Alien Worker,
seeking EB-1A classification as an individual of extraordinary ability. I intend to continue my
professional work in the United States in IT project management in the field of urban digital
infrastructure, innovation and delivery for local governments.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 28--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">I will build a consulting and product practice dedicated to municipal IT project management and
execution. The practice will deliver incident and service management platforms modeled on my prior
NextITSM architecture and the operating model developed and proven at iKOMEK 2.0. Each
engagement will apply disciplined delivery mechanics, requirements baselining and scope control,
governance charters, KPI and service level agreement (SLA) taxonomies, risk, issue and change
management, iterative release trains, data quality and machine learning operations (MLOps)
pipelines, and security by design to ensure schedule, budget and benefit realization in production
environments.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 32--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">I plan to collaborate directly with U.S. municipalities to adapt, implement and manage Smart City
components that I have validated in practice, using modern IT project management methods and
tooling, Agile delivery, KPI and service level agreement (SLA) governance, continuous integration and
continuous delivery (CI/CD), and machine learning operations (MLOps) to achieve-Goals efficiently and
expeditiously. Initial deployments will prioritize (i) a cloud platform for omnichannel citizen request
intake, routing and service level agreement (SLA) tracking, (ii) artificial intelligence (AI)
assisted triage and analytics for pattern detection and demand forecasting, (iii) video analytics
for public safety and operations use cases, and (iv) executive dashboards for transparent
performance management. These solutions are particularly relevant for jurisdictions up to
approximately 1 million residents, where budgets are constrained but the need for digitalization is
acute.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 34--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">In parallel, I will launch a pilot “Smart Response” program with one U.S. city, adapting the iKOMEK
approach to local constraints. The platform will follow low code principles, use an open source first
modular stack, and offer a flexible licensing model to keep total cost of ownership low and long term
operations sustainable for local administrations. This work is designed to deliver tangible
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
outcomes for problems common to small and mid sized cities, including overloaded municipal
services, the lack of a unified digital environment for receiving and resolving resident requests,
fragmented data, and outdated channels between residents and administration. The same
methods and architectures that proved effective in my prior programs can be adapted to U.S.
conditions to close this technology gap, accelerating digitalization of city infrastructure,
improving management efficiency and lowering cost to serve, thereby benefiting the United
States.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 36--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">The implementation of my projects will directly contribute to job creation and the strengthening
of economic activity. In the course of this work, I plan to hire professionals in key areas,
including project managers, analysts, data engineers, implementation specialists and technical
support staff. This will generate formal employment, increase tax revenues and provide a
direct economic benefit. Part of these teams will be established in mid sized cities using a
hybrid work model that combines on site and remote participation. This approach enables the
creation of jobs and economic activity not only in major metropolitan areas but also in cities
with population up to one million residents, ensuring a stable and positive impact on local
economies.
</text:p> 
<!--l. 38--><text:p text:style-name="Text-body">This plan represents a direct continuation of my established professional path in IT infrastructure
development, digital governance and economic efficiency. My work in the United States will contribute
by improving municipal systems, strengthening cybersecurity practices, creating jobs in underserved
regions and notably enhancing the quality and responsiveness of city services. With my expertise as an
IT project manager, I am well positioned to execute this plan effectively and achieve its stated
goals.
</text:p> 
<text:section text:style-name="begin-end-env" text:name="begin-end-env-6" ><text:p text:style-name="begin-env-p" ></text:p><!--begin flushright-->
<text:p text:style-name="flushright" >
 <text:span text:style-name="textbf" ><text:span 
text:style-name="ecbx-1200">Sincerely,</text:span></text:span> 
</text:p><text:p text:style-name="flushright" >Askar Taximov
</text:p><text:p text:style-name="end-env-p" ></text:p></text:section><!--end flushright-->
                                                                                              
                                                                                              
